  ('15c2ceb8-4668-56e7-bd60-280a81dc534a'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'A real gift from your browser', 'An official CBSE scholarship', 'A Windows system update', 'a', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'A genuine prize because a flashing pop-up proves that an online offer is real', 'A verified scholarship that is safe to claim by entering personal details into any form linked from the pop-up', 'An official Windows security update that always requires a personal address before you may close its window'),
  ('87c83290-5ec2-569a-a24e-baced1582a67'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Netiquette"?', 'A brand of Ethernet cable', 'Good manners, kindness, and respectful behavior when communicating on the internet', 'An offline calculator game', 'A type of mosquito net', 'b', 'What is "Netiquette"?', 'The technical standard for connecting a computer to a wired Ethernet network at a school', 'Good manners, kindness, and respectful behavior when communicating on the internet', 'The rule that internet accounts must remain private and never send messages to other users', 'The software that automatically corrects grammar and spelling in every online message'),
  ('66a74e93-5c31-5e86-aec7-7d2d39066c16'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'Yes, if they have a cool profile picture', 'Yes, on every public comment section', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes, if they offer free game coins', 'c', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'Yes — if a stranger has a friendly picture on their profile', 'Yes — whenever a game chat is visible to the public', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes — if the stranger promises you free coins in the game'),
  ('7b717bf1-05a4-5113-bf56-f781152cfabb'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Never use books or references', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'd', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Use the work without credit as long as it is found through a search engine and used in a school project', 'Link to a source only when the creator is personally known to you, even when their license requires credit', 'Remove the creator''s name from the image and present the work as entirely original to your own team', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself'),
  ('4fed2b36-ec63-575d-8e0a-c82cf3fd5447'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'd', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Once every 20 hours, look at a screen from a distance of 20 millimetres for 20 seconds without a break', 'Every 20 minutes, move the screen 20 cm closer and stare for 20 minutes', 'Every 20 minutes, blink exactly 20 times while keeping your eyes fixed on the screen for 20 seconds', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes'),
  ('54bed9e4-33e6-5f09-873b-2b0bc3f0c312'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'b', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'Receiving a gift requires the recipient to scan a payment request and enter the UPI PIN', 'Never enter or share your UPI PIN to receive money; any request to do so is a scam.', 'The recipient must share their UPI PIN with the sender to receive an ordinary payment', 'An incoming UPI transfer needs the recipient''s PIN before the money can reach their account'),
  ('50d6ff99-ceae-565b-b7f6-f4f808b727f5'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'c', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It needs two passwords in one box without asking for a second device, code or security key', 'It replaces the password with two public usernames, so knowing the account name alone is enough to sign in from any device online', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It lets anyone with a leaked password receive the second code automatically, without the account owner''s approval'),
  ('c9e6a189-13d3-5545-b2a5-5bb8cf31426b'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'There is zero risk', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'a', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'A reused password takes extra storage on every device, which is the only security concern to consider', 'An attack on one small game site cannot affect another account, even when the same leaked password is reused across all websites and email services', 'Web browsers permanently block accounts that reuse a password, so there is no chance of unauthorized access'),
  ('338c4573-d767-5401-a0f8-9082761c0dec'::uuid, 6, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'a', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Use AI to produce the complete project, submit its wording unchanged, and claim every idea was independently your own work', 'Use AI as a source of final facts because checking dates, quotations and sources is unnecessary when the answer sounds confident, regardless of your teacher''s rules', 'Use AI during a closed-book test without asking whether its use is allowed and describe all the answers as your own understanding');
