  ('7b96fd35-6f88-568d-b05b-20c81d58dafd'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Internet plan speeds from providers like JioFiber, Airtel, or BSNL are commonly advertised in "100 Mbps". What does Mbps measure?', 'How many months the plan lasts', 'Megabits per second — how fast data transfers over your internet connection', 'How far the Wi-Fi reaches in meters', 'How many devices are allowed', 'b', 'Internet plan speeds from providers like JioFiber, Airtel, or BSNL are commonly advertised in "100 Mbps". What does Mbps measure?', 'The number of monthly payments a customer must make before the broadband service plan expires', 'Megabits per second — the rate at which data can transfer across an internet connection each second', 'The number of metres a wireless signal can travel before it reaches a wall or another obstacle', 'The maximum number of devices allowed to connect to the router during one billing month'),
  ('2122c20a-e2d9-5d4d-9a44-1325aecb2f2e'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Companies like BSNL, Airtel, Jio, or local fiber broadband providers that connect homes/schools to the internet are called:', 'Search Engines', 'Operating Systems', 'ISPs (Internet Service Providers)', 'Web Browsers', 'c', 'Companies like BSNL, Airtel, Jio, or local fiber broadband providers that connect homes/schools to the internet are called:', 'Internet Search Engine Services', 'Computer Operating Systems', 'ISPs (Internet Service Providers)', 'Website Browsing Applications'),
  ('98284578-b754-5238-b498-aa882c21d72d'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why does Wi-Fi signal become weaker when you walk three rooms away behind thick concrete walls?', 'Gravity pulls Wi-Fi down', 'The phone screen gets smaller', 'Wi-Fi needs sunlight to travel', 'Thick walls and distance absorb and weaken wireless radio waves from the router', 'd', 'Why does Wi-Fi signal become weaker when you walk three rooms away behind thick concrete walls?', 'The router transmits weaker radio waves whenever a phone changes rooms even if the distance remains identical', 'Concrete walls boost the signal but the phone blocks the excess strength to keep it from overheating', 'The radio signal stays equally strong through concrete, but the phone displays fewer Wi-Fi bars', 'Thick walls and distance absorb and weaken wireless radio waves from the router'),
  ('7b970d28-c49c-56aa-a121-e9e868e66563'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is a "Local Area Network (LAN)" in simple everyday words?', 'Satellites orbiting Mars', 'A type of USB pendrive', 'An antivirus program', 'Computers, laptops, and printers connected together inside one building, home, or school campus', 'd', 'What is a "Local Area Network (LAN)" in simple everyday words?', 'A group of satellites orbiting the Earth to provide worldwide internet access to mobile phones', 'A pocket-sized storage drive plugged into one computer to carry files between different buildings', 'An antivirus application that removes all viruses automatically without using a computer network', 'Computers, laptops, and printers connected together inside one building, home, or school campus'),
  ('99eafc37-5b95-57d6-97d7-674131330c73'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'b', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only the computer connected to the printer by an HDMI cable can send documents to it', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'No computer can print at all because printers connected through Wi-Fi cannot receive documents wirelessly', 'Only phones without a SIM card can use the printer over the school''s wireless network'),
  ('7234e324-31e3-53ce-8861-8950b181847f'::uuid, 7, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Disk Formatting', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'Zipping', 'c', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Private Browsing / Incognito Mode', 'Drive Formatting / Disk Erasing', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'File Compression / Zip Archive'),
  ('b7385ca6-28f9-5aaa-b423-3d57410fac01'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'In online group chats or comments, typing an entire message IN ALL CAPITAL LETTERS LIKE THIS is usually read as:', 'Encrypting the message', 'Whispering politely', 'SHOUTING or being rude online', 'Writing faster', 'c', 'In online group chats or comments, typing an entire message IN ALL CAPITAL LETTERS LIKE THIS is usually read as:', 'An encrypted and private message', 'A gentle and quiet speaking tone', 'SHOUTING or being rude online', 'A faster way to type a message'),
  ('8905fe52-fe98-52d9-86de-5ad77401504d'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a junior student asks a very basic computer question in the tech club, how should a good member respond?', 'Explain it patiently and kindly — everyone starts as a beginner!', 'Tell them to quit computers', 'Ignore them completely', 'Laugh at them in front of the group', 'a', 'If a junior student asks a very basic computer question in the tech club, how should a good member respond?', 'Explain it patiently and kindly — everyone starts as a beginner!', 'Tell them to quit the club until they understand every basic task', 'Ask them to search alone and not ask anyone else in the group for help', 'Laugh at their question in front of the rest of the group'),
  ('86ba0d9d-adcc-5d10-b530-351a5fb9e354'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If someone repeatedly sends mean, hurtful, or threatening messages to a classmate online, what is that harmful behavior called?', 'Cyberbullying (which must be reported to parents/teachers, never joined!)', 'Cloud Computing', 'Web Browsing', 'Troubleshooting', 'a', 'If someone repeatedly sends mean, hurtful, or threatening messages to a classmate online, what is that harmful behavior called?', 'Cyberbullying (which must be reported to parents/teachers, never joined!)', 'Cloud computing — using network servers to store and process information', 'Web browsing — visiting and reading pages on internet websites', 'Technical troubleshooting — fixing problems with a device or network'),
  ('6c76845f-c828-5f4f-a0f4-1e065ea4a860'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'You receive a dramatic WhatsApp forward saying "Tomorrow is a sudden holiday — forward to 20 friends!" What is the smart, responsible step?', 'Forward it to 50 groups immediately', 'Do NOT forward blindly — verify first from the official school notice or teacher', 'Skip homework without checking', 'Post it as breaking news', 'b', 'You receive a dramatic WhatsApp forward saying "Tomorrow is a sudden holiday — forward to 20 friends!" What is the smart, responsible step?', 'Forward the announcement to every class group first, then verify it only after several friends repeat the same claim', 'Do NOT forward blindly — verify first from the official school notice or teacher', 'Skip homework immediately because any message containing a holiday date is automatically an official school announcement', 'Post it as confirmed breaking news if the sender sounds confident, even without an official school notice'),
  ('a4d1fe20-a1c3-57f8-af52-aae9d7808ac1'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why shouldn’t you eat sticky snacks or keep an open cup of water right over a computer keyboard?', 'Water changes the wallpaper', 'Snacks reduce Wi-Fi bars', 'Crumbs and spilled liquid can permanently short-circuit and ruin the keyboard or laptop', 'Food slows down Google Search', 'c', 'Why shouldn’t you eat sticky snacks or keep an open cup of water right over a computer keyboard?', 'Spilled water changes the wallpaper but cannot harm the circuits of a powered computer', 'Food on the keyboard boosts Wi-Fi signals and improves the internet connection', 'Crumbs and spilled liquid can permanently short-circuit and ruin the keyboard or laptop', 'Crumbs and liquid affect the screen brightness but cannot damage the hardware'),
  ('38861554-8095-53f5-a210-860f99776766'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'A Windows system update', 'An official CBSE scholarship', 'A real gift from your browser', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'd', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'An official Windows security update that always requires a personal address before you may close its window', 'A verified scholarship that is safe to claim by entering personal details into any form linked from the pop-up', 'A genuine prize because a flashing pop-up proves that an online offer is real', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!'),
  ('12827728-75ac-5ff1-b73f-a16ef59fcb0a'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Netiquette"?', 'A brand of Ethernet cable', 'A type of mosquito net', 'An offline calculator game', 'Good manners, kindness, and respectful behavior when communicating on the internet', 'd', 'What is "Netiquette"?', 'The technical standard for connecting a computer to a wired Ethernet network at a school', 'The software that automatically corrects grammar and spelling in every online message', 'The rule that internet accounts must remain private and never send messages to other users', 'Good manners, kindness, and respectful behavior when communicating on the internet'),
  ('24a10f6c-92be-531d-963f-c01a8371307a'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'Yes, if they have a cool profile picture', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes, if they offer free game coins', 'Yes, on every public comment section', 'b', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'Yes — if a stranger has a friendly picture on their profile', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes — if the stranger promises you free coins in the game', 'Yes — whenever a game chat is visible to the public'),
  ('dfde707a-f8a7-53e2-a081-0ad991aedd0c'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Never use books or references', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'c', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Use the work without credit as long as it is found through a search engine and used in a school project', 'Remove the creator''s name from the image and present the work as entirely original to your own team', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'Link to a source only when the creator is personally known to you, even when their license requires credit'),
  ('650a9712-0593-5c0b-baa9-1444dc70c5ce'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'a', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Every 20 minutes, move the screen 20 cm closer and stare for 20 minutes', 'Every 20 minutes, blink exactly 20 times while keeping your eyes fixed on the screen for 20 seconds', 'Once every 20 hours, look at a screen from a distance of 20 millimetres for 20 seconds without a break'),
  ('3b3fd586-b2b8-5f5a-b96b-b8095bf8f111'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'a', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'Never enter or share your UPI PIN to receive money; any request to do so is a scam.', 'The recipient must share their UPI PIN with the sender to receive an ordinary payment', 'Receiving a gift requires the recipient to scan a payment request and enter the UPI PIN', 'An incoming UPI transfer needs the recipient''s PIN before the money can reach their account'),
  ('c99f8a58-819a-52c0-825d-ea314e805ed9'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'b', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It replaces the password with two public usernames, so knowing the account name alone is enough to sign in from any device online', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It needs two passwords in one box without asking for a second device, code or security key', 'It lets anyone with a leaked password receive the second code automatically, without the account owner''s approval'),
  ('bf4b331b-13fa-5a9b-86e9-3bab24cd0b22'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'There is zero risk', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'c', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'A reused password takes extra storage on every device, which is the only security concern to consider', 'An attack on one small game site cannot affect another account, even when the same leaked password is reused across all websites and email services', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Web browsers permanently block accounts that reuse a password, so there is no chance of unauthorized access'),
  ('84b2a821-e3dc-5e43-953f-8f86fee9da43'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'd', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during a closed-book test without asking whether its use is allowed and describe all the answers as your own understanding', 'Use AI as a source of final facts because checking dates, quotations and sources is unnecessary when the answer sounds confident, regardless of your teacher''s rules', 'Use AI to produce the complete project, submit its wording unchanged, and claim every idea was independently your own work', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped'),
  ('fe077f3b-bef4-5a83-9739-12167270318a'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Allow everything without reading', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'd', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Allow all app permissions because it cannot collect or share your contacts or messages without asking you a second time first', 'Allow access to contacts because the camera LED needs phone numbers in order to illuminate a room properly', 'Allow microphone and message access because installing any app guarantees that all its permissions are required', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag'),
  ('887dd13d-27dc-5bdd-a72c-285c69b7e92d'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Testing internet speed', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'b', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'A routine process in which a legitimate company asks every user to post their password publicly for other people to read without any checks or consent', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'A trusted internet service measuring the speed of a connection without asking for private account details or one-time passwords', 'Software that scans a computer''s storage for viruses and removes any infected files that it happens to find on the device'),
  ('e239d343-c226-55ac-b691-b800ba5af1c7'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'c', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The physical fingerprints used by a device''s biometric sensor to unlock a phone or laptop', 'The total amount of electrical power used by your computer whenever it accesses the internet', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The private record of files stored on a device with no activity shared through an online account'),
  ('97c1df29-da1a-55ce-93e1-0cb8f8132b37'::uuid, 7, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'a', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked programs are guaranteed to be safer than official versions because they skip all security updates', 'Free legal alternatives cannot exist, so downloading a paid application''s crack is the only lawful option', 'Unofficial cracks are automatically scanned, approved and regularly updated by the original software creator before every download from a third-party website');
INSERT INTO pg_temp.mtc_revised_seed_20261030 VALUES
  ('28284fbc-1c4c-54a6-a68d-16f5ba9febf5'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut CUTS (moves) selected text so you can paste it somewhere else?', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + X', 'Ctrl + K', 'Ctrl + M', 'b', 'Which shortcut CUTS (moves) selected text so you can paste it somewhere else?', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + X', 'Ctrl + K', 'Ctrl + M'),
  ('96d6df6a-0c59-5418-af71-40e66e831236'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'While watching a video on YouTube or VLC, pressing the Spacebar usually does what?', 'Pauses or plays the video', 'Deletes the video', 'Prints the screen', 'Shuts down the computer', 'a', 'While watching a video on YouTube or VLC, pressing the Spacebar usually does what?', 'Pauses or plays the video', 'Deletes the current video file', 'Captures the current screen image', 'Turns off the computer'),
  ('4051e63b-fa2a-53f1-831f-c2fcb2cb5009'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens the PRINT box to print a page or save it as a PDF?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + P', 'Ctrl + R', 'c', 'Which shortcut opens the PRINT box to print a page or save it as a PDF?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + P', 'Ctrl + R'),
  ('bb280d5c-a1e3-53ec-8173-c46206db8744'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In Word or Google Docs, what does pressing Ctrl + B do to selected text?', 'Moves text to the bottom', 'Deletes the text', 'Turns the text Blue', 'Makes the text Bold (thicker)', 'd', 'In Word or Google Docs, what does pressing Ctrl + B do to selected text?', 'Moves the text to the bottom', 'Makes the selected text smaller', 'Changes the text colour to blue', 'Makes the text Bold (thicker)'),
  ('15de69da-c052-5753-bd6e-b75ce9a35e24'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + U', 'a', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + I', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + U'),
  ('63f114ea-b226-567b-a0e4-5678271183d9'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + O', 'c', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + O'),
  ('c9e6d9b6-b6d9-5bf3-954e-ee38dc0d8c38'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace closes the program', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Both do the exact same thing', 'Delete only works on images', 'b', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace erases the character on the right of the cursor; Delete erases the one on the left', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Backspace erases a whole line at once; Delete erases a whole paragraph at once', 'Backspace removes only selected images; Delete removes only selected text in the document'),
  ('289e1dc7-0290-597c-a38e-b2eaa313c929'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + G', 'a', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + G'),
  ('34cefeb1-90b9-5575-a1b1-cf2c65e8aa89'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Tab', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Insert', 'Num Lock', 'b', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Num Lock key', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Del (Delete)', 'Ins (Insert)'),
  ('ac28f38f-0617-5c75-8f13-e672afb68c08'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F2', 'F1', 'F12', 'F5', 'd', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F2', 'F1', 'F12', 'F5'),
  ('fa0b991a-4980-578b-af65-21938e959475'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + E', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'c', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + E', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R'),
  ('5a0e9383-6b2d-5c95-b569-addcc9928b41'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Ctrl + P', 'Shift + Enter', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C', 'c', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Ctrl + P', 'Shift + Enter', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C'),
  ('191393a4-a631-5513-9c2a-7de90b875543'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Ctrl', 'Shift', 'Tab', 'Alt', 'b', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Space', 'Shift', 'Enter', 'AltGr'),
  ('34e9a7cc-cfde-560c-bb20-0262b15b82f8'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + D', 'b', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + D'),
  ('5a49ff18-c826-5404-b45d-fb139e5528f6'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Closes the browser', 'Translates the page', 'b', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Turns off Wi-Fi access', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Closes the current browser tab', 'Translates the current page'),
  ('ec88a1dc-95d4-55cb-bcfc-e0ec774fe6dc'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Turns the screen white', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'a', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Turns the browser screen white', 'Saves bookmarks in this tab', 'Opens the Microsoft Word app'),
  ('e062ad01-56d3-5b5a-ab07-8c29910f5fda'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Scroll Lock', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Page Down', 'Pause/Break', 'b', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'ScrLk (Scroll Lock key)', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'PgDn (Page Down key)', 'Pause or Break key'),
  ('208cf845-0a4d-5c18-aab8-c3e364977c18'::uuid, 8, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F1', 'F8', 'F4', 'a', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F1', 'F8', 'F4'),
  ('a9edd9ec-6224-51d6-b335-a1767d4e138b'::uuid, 8, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which pocket-sized device plugs into a USB port to carry files between home and school?', 'Mouse Pad', 'USB Pendrive (Flash Drive)', 'Cooling Fan', 'UPS Battery', 'b', 'Which pocket-sized device plugs into a USB port to carry files between home and school?', 'Flexible laptop mouse pad', 'USB Pendrive (Flash Drive)', 'Portable notebook cooling fan', 'Desktop UPS battery backup'),
