  ('626b3480-a1a3-50de-a495-99b14b1301f6'::uuid, 8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'd', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It increases the brightness of the laptop screen and keeps the display awake for longer', 'It permanently doubles keyboard speed whenever the laptop uses a mobile hotspot', 'It uninstalls all browsers automatically so the laptop cannot use the internet connection', 'It can limit large background updates and downloads, helping reduce mobile data use.'),
  ('92223716-ad41-5e7a-8056-4d711d4d80b0'::uuid, 8, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', 'There is no difference at all', 'b', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', 'The 2.4 GHz wireless network works only when the current time is exactly 2:40 in the afternoon', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', 'The 5 GHz Wi-Fi network works only if the home router has a 5G mobile SIM card inside', 'Both networks always have the same speed and range, regardless of walls or distance'),
  ('25bdf8d9-35e6-5af4-8da3-2f8c7dbee14b'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why shouldn’t you eat sticky snacks or keep an open cup of water right over a computer keyboard?', 'Water changes the wallpaper', 'Crumbs and spilled liquid can permanently short-circuit and ruin the keyboard or laptop', 'Food slows down Google Search', 'Snacks reduce Wi-Fi bars', 'b', 'Why shouldn’t you eat sticky snacks or keep an open cup of water right over a computer keyboard?', 'Spilled water changes the wallpaper but cannot harm the circuits of a powered computer', 'Crumbs and spilled liquid can permanently short-circuit and ruin the keyboard or laptop', 'Crumbs and liquid affect the screen brightness but cannot damage the hardware', 'Food on the keyboard boosts Wi-Fi signals and improves the internet connection'),
  ('189eb84c-5499-5f60-a7fc-ec711bfeab10'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'A Windows system update', 'A real gift from your browser', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'An official CBSE scholarship', 'c', 'If a pop-up flashes on screen: "🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! You won a free iPhone! Click here & enter your details!", what is it almost certainly?', 'An official Windows security update that always requires a personal address before you may close its window', 'A genuine prize because a flashing pop-up proves that an online offer is real', 'A scam / phishing trap trying to steal personal details or install malware — close it immediately!', 'A verified scholarship that is safe to claim by entering personal details into any form linked from the pop-up'),
