  ('8d25b683-c7ea-5af5-a179-d6a22c2eb11e'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes, if they offer free game coins', 'Yes, if they have a cool profile picture', 'Yes, on every public comment section', 'a', 'Should you share your home address, school timetable, and phone number publicly with unknown strangers in online game chats?', 'No — keep personal details private to stay safe online', 'Yes — if the stranger promises you free coins in the game', 'Yes — if a stranger has a friendly picture on their profile', 'Yes — whenever a game chat is visible to the public'),
  ('931b2765-b99e-56b1-ab16-0e139b5e06bc'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'Never use books or references', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'b', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Remove the creator''s name from the image and present the work as entirely original to your own team', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'Use the work without credit as long as it is found through a search engine and used in a school project', 'Link to a source only when the creator is personally known to you, even when their license requires credit'),
  ('e2da24d3-2399-5ee9-9c6f-4db805947540'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'c', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Every 20 minutes, move the screen 20 cm closer and stare for 20 minutes', 'Every 20 minutes, blink exactly 20 times while keeping your eyes fixed on the screen for 20 seconds', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Once every 20 hours, look at a screen from a distance of 20 millimetres for 20 seconds without a break'),
  ('c171b3e7-d2d1-501e-b95b-01034938fd21'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'd', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'An incoming UPI transfer needs the recipient''s PIN before the money can reach their account', 'Receiving a gift requires the recipient to scan a payment request and enter the UPI PIN', 'The recipient must share their UPI PIN with the sender to receive an ordinary payment', 'Never enter or share your UPI PIN to receive money; any request to do so is a scam.'),
  ('a722820f-72a1-563d-85c0-ff1997e1e93d'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'd', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It replaces the password with two public usernames, so knowing the account name alone is enough to sign in from any device online', 'It lets anyone with a leaked password receive the second code automatically, without the account owner''s approval', 'It needs two passwords in one box without asking for a second device, code or security key', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone'),
  ('6b178e79-220f-51e0-b856-febf1ee37b80'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'There is zero risk', 'b', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'A reused password takes extra storage on every device, which is the only security concern to consider', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Web browsers permanently block accounts that reuse a password, so there is no chance of unauthorized access', 'An attack on one small game site cannot affect another account, even when the same leaked password is reused across all websites and email services'),
  ('b4bbb927-7b0a-54a8-b10c-b6f57bf78c28'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'c', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI during a closed-book test without asking whether its use is allowed and describe all the answers as your own understanding', 'Use AI to produce the complete project, submit its wording unchanged, and claim every idea was independently your own work', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Use AI as a source of final facts because checking dates, quotations and sources is unnecessary when the answer sounds confident, regardless of your teacher''s rules'),
  ('e40e1019-5ccf-533d-8d7d-04b93fb8ee8f'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Allow everything without reading', 'a', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow access to contacts because the camera LED needs phone numbers in order to illuminate a room properly', 'Allow microphone and message access because installing any app guarantees that all its permissions are required', 'Allow all app permissions because it cannot collect or share your contacts or messages without asking you a second time first'),
  ('5e86c318-0430-5ff9-8e24-277d89858020'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Testing internet speed', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'a', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'A trusted internet service measuring the speed of a connection without asking for private account details or one-time passwords', 'A routine process in which a legitimate company asks every user to post their password publicly for other people to read without any checks or consent', 'Software that scans a computer''s storage for viruses and removes any infected files that it happens to find on the device'),
  ('67f587b2-05b6-522c-8c32-4357960bec6d'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'b', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The total amount of electrical power used by your computer whenever it accesses the internet', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The physical fingerprints used by a device''s biometric sensor to unlock a phone or laptop', 'The private record of files stored on a device with no activity shared through an online account'),
  ('c51d7af0-ace2-5462-8e81-fe422fc995a9'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'c', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Cracked programs are guaranteed to be safer than official versions because they skip all security updates', 'Free legal alternatives cannot exist, so downloading a paid application''s crack is the only lawful option', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Unofficial cracks are automatically scanned, approved and regularly updated by the original software creator before every download from a third-party website'),
  ('b0f70ccc-b77b-548a-9476-930942d16dc2'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'd', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click Save and trust that the next person cannot view or reuse a password stored on a shared school computer', 'Click Save for this session only, because saved passwords are deleted when another user opens the browser', 'Click Save but sign out afterwards, because closing the tab always deletes any saved account credentials', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!'),
  ('543f222c-bac0-5168-ab8d-3a0bcb127da2'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'd', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Send repeated stickers late at night as long as one useful study message follows', 'Debate classmates'' personal problems publicly in the group whenever the argument involves someone from class', 'Send unverified reminders and rumours to the whole class first, and confirm them only if a teacher complains', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions'),
  ('a8c0f8ba-038f-5d89-90dc-aa85e0c371d2'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To slow down your internet', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To erase your photos', 'b', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Increase internet download speeds by replacing the Wi-Fi hardware with a faster network chip', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Add new visual themes and icon colours even when no security flaws or software problems are being fixed', 'Remove every personal file so the device can no longer be infected by malicious attachments'),
  ('ffd87270-54d9-546f-b84b-484eda7b17a6'::uuid, 8, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Change their account password', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'c', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Read a few recent emails to check whether the account is important, then sign out and tell the classmate afterward', 'Change the password to protect the account, then tell the classmate that the new login details are a surprise', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a harmless message from their account to inform the class, then sign out when the computer is no longer needed');
INSERT INTO pg_temp.mtc_revised_seed_20261030 VALUES
  ('2e5c8193-5315-5344-beb0-73237425f50c'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + I', 'd', 'In a document editor, which shortcut makes selected text Italic (slanted)?', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + L', 'Ctrl + T', 'Ctrl + I'),
  ('b42d2859-dfbe-50d4-bccf-c687db973574'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + O', 'b', 'In a document editor, which shortcut UNDERLINES the selected words?', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + U', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + O'),
  ('8e9e0270-6c90-5a58-b765-c91d16f7b20e'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Both do the exact same thing', 'Backspace closes the program', 'Delete only works on images', 'a', 'What is the difference between the Backspace key and the Delete key while typing?', 'Backspace erases to the left of the cursor; Delete erases to the right of the cursor', 'Backspace erases a whole line at once; Delete erases a whole paragraph at once', 'Backspace erases the character on the right of the cursor; Delete erases the one on the left', 'Backspace removes only selected images; Delete removes only selected text in the document'),
  ('9639dd13-54af-5113-9e2d-3455f127ea31'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + G', 'c', 'If you want to quickly FIND a specific word on a long webpage or PDF, which shortcut do you press?', 'Ctrl + H', 'Ctrl + Q', 'Ctrl + F', 'Ctrl + G'),
  ('535d7c30-7b4c-5efb-8603-c38f3c2bd851'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Num Lock', 'Insert', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Tab', 'c', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Ins (Insert)', 'Del (Delete)', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Num Lock key'),
  ('5a2faaf1-9d00-5850-8ee2-481bbf15d102'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F2', 'F5', 'F12', 'F1', 'b', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F2', 'F5', 'F12', 'F1'),
  ('ec4939b5-4ce4-59dd-a03c-2606ca624b6c'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + E', 'b', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + E'),
