  ('61935299-c984-511f-921a-4b114e1d8670'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the screen white', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'c', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the browser screen white', 'Saves bookmarks in this tab', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens the Microsoft Word app'),
  ('cdc2e94a-8d22-5538-9c8a-cfddab4c7fdf'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause/Break', 'Page Down', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'c', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause or Break key', 'PgDn (Page Down key)', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'ScrLk (Scroll Lock key)'),
  ('54c440ca-fbb6-5461-aa89-449087601215'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1', 'a', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F2', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1'),
  ('7d74a21a-ec6c-5147-8416-9c25e282bb41'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Increases speaker volume', 'Opens four new folders', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'c', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Increases the volume of the current app', 'Opens four folders in the current application', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Enables Bluetooth on the current PC'),
  ('fd96ad43-8e80-5993-a379-371059c3af5a'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Opens calculator', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Adds a new user account', 'Increases internet speed', 'b', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Opens the calculator beside the current webpage', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Creates a new account for the current web browser user', 'Increases the speed of the internet connection'),
  ('fbc6ba34-86b0-5a9b-b1c4-4b86a2eed5cf'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Closes all tabs', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'd', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Clears all the pages that are stored in browser history', 'Turns off sound for every open application', 'Resets the zoom level for every browser tab', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)'),
  ('a9b99873-e54f-5446-aa96-76aed012dfc0'::uuid, 9, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Erases what you typed', 'Closes the browser tab', 'b', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Submits the form and sends every answer to the server', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Clears the answer from the currently active input box', 'Moves the cursor to the previous input box'),
  ('2dc551a8-e0d7-56bf-b5bc-dcbd568bf49a'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'On a smartphone or tablet, the screen both shows pictures AND senses your finger taps. What is it called?', 'Touchscreen', 'Plotter', 'Joystick', 'Barcode Reader', 'a', 'On a smartphone or tablet, the screen both shows pictures AND senses your finger taps. What is it called?', 'Touchscreen', 'Plotter', 'Joystick', 'Barcode Reader'),
  ('e2cefa10-9e55-5cdf-a8f3-e0b876362040'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What Does "Hardware" mean in simple everyday words?', 'The physical parts of a computer that you can actually see and touch', 'Only paid mobile games', 'Secret passwords', 'Websites on the internet', 'a', 'What Does "Hardware" mean in simple everyday words?', 'The physical parts of a computer that you can actually see and touch', 'The apps and operating system that control the computer''s everyday work', 'The secret passwords and access codes used to unlock computer software', 'The internet sites and online services that are visited by a user from a computer'),
  ('f38939ff-1a78-55b0-b4a2-9bb9bcdf5467'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In Indian homes and school labs, a small box called a UPS is connected to desktop PCs. Why is it useful?', 'It prints color photos', 'It cleans computer viruses', 'It makes games run faster', 'It provides short battery backup during a power cut so you can save your work safely', 'd', 'In Indian homes and school labs, a small box called a UPS is connected to desktop PCs. Why is it useful?', 'It increases the speed of games by adding extra working memory to the connected computer system', 'It gives the computer a faster internet connection by creating a new private wireless network at home', 'It cleans malware from every stored file whenever power is switched on', 'It provides short battery backup during a power cut so you can save your work safely'),
  ('e9146af8-61f4-52a6-93a9-595d47681f59'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the opposite of a Printer — a device that turns a paper certificate or drawing into a digital image file on your PC?', 'Modem', 'Projector', 'Scanner', 'Speaker', 'c', 'What is the opposite of a Printer — a device that turns a paper certificate or drawing into a digital image file on your PC?', 'Modem', 'Projector', 'Scanner', 'Speaker'),
  ('55739e1b-26e1-5e16-82b5-17c5b643cdc4'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which single modern cable carries BOTH sharp high-definition video AND audio from a laptop to a TV or projector?', 'Power cord', 'Mouse wire', 'Earphone jack', 'HDMI cable', 'd', 'Which single modern cable carries BOTH sharp high-definition video AND audio from a laptop to a TV or projector?', 'Power cord', 'Mouse wire', 'Earphone jack', 'HDMI cable'),
  ('098e16cf-1146-58ba-970a-766800e88e2f'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'At a supermarket checkout or school library, which handheld device reads black-and-white striped labels instantly?', 'Joystick', 'Barcode Scanner', 'Microphone', 'Cooling Pad', 'b', 'At a supermarket checkout or school library, which handheld device reads black-and-white striped labels instantly?', 'RFID Card Reader', 'Barcode Scanner', 'Fingerprint Pad', 'Magnetic Reader'),
  ('96b6a7ca-53ff-5b2f-8697-0df8b671b30e'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Why can a laptop keep running during a power cut even without an external UPS?', 'The keyboard generates power', 'Laptops have a built-in rechargeable battery inside', 'Laptops do not use electricity', 'Laptops run on Wi-Fi waves', 'b', 'Why can a laptop keep running during a power cut even without an external UPS?', 'Key presses generate enough electricity to power it', 'Laptops have a built-in rechargeable battery inside', 'Wi-Fi signals directly power laptops during outages', 'The cable supplies stored power during outages'),
  ('12044f2f-4841-5f8d-981f-29ad7bd43cad'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the tiny removable storage card used inside many cameras and Android phones called?', 'SIM card', 'Credit card', 'Graphics card', 'MicroSD (Memory) card', 'd', 'What is the tiny removable storage card used inside many cameras and Android phones called?', 'Contactless payment card', 'Wireless mobile SIM card', 'Computer graphics card', 'MicroSD Flash Memory Card'),
  ('da00a3ae-90a9-5c67-8d69-9db5a726794f'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To make music louder', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'b', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To remove dust from the laptop without changing its internal temperature', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To supply battery power by turning the spinning fan into electrical current', 'To increase the processor''s computing performance by supplying it with extra electrical current'),
  ('f364a432-11e7-573a-ae48-f1582c8d7dce'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'RAM is only for printers', 'Both are names for the screen', 'b', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM is found only in printers and holds photos forever; Storage erases all of its contents after every restart', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'RAM and Storage both refer to the screen, and neither has any role in keeping data or running applications', 'RAM stores files permanently when powered off; Storage holds open apps only until the computer is shut down'),
  ('d191a40c-2520-5182-9154-f2539fe28140'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A louder speaker', 'A longer power cable', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'RAM (working memory)', 'd', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'Wi-Fi network modem', 'Graphics processor', 'Internal SSD drive', 'RAM (working memory)'),
  ('9cb3d7d5-6a1a-5aa9-8833-fc47d9281716'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'It prints paper automatically', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'The screen becomes wider', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'd', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'It automatically increases available RAM for every app without changing any memory modules in the laptop', 'It improves Wi-Fi coverage even if all the wireless network hardware remains completely unchanged', 'It removes the need for backups because an SSD can never fail or lose data', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts'),
  ('9621e46f-cbcc-566d-9cdb-eee471a2548d'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'VGA port', 'PS/2 round port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'd', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'VGA display port', 'Optical CD-ROM slot', 'PS/2 keyboard port', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)'),
  ('ec48266b-f568-50a9-ac07-a81fb09f54bb'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Clipboard', 'Whiteboard', 'Motherboard', 'Dashboard', 'c', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Memory card', 'Cooling fan', 'Motherboard', 'Graphics card'),
  ('223c533a-1c68-5c6e-9ff0-108ac5010af3'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Delete your files', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'Buy a new monitor', 'b', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Delete files because a full disk means the mouse cannot work at all in any app', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'Reinstall Windows first because the mouse battery cannot affect movement of the screen pointer', 'Replace the monitor first because the pointer is always controlled by the display hardware'),
  ('2f2f7590-6733-53bd-89e2-8956541b708b'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Router antenna', 'Thumb drive', 'Laser printer', 'a', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Trackpad', 'Joystick', 'Mouse'),
  ('ea188026-8cab-5d81-a2f4-99facac7ac22'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', 'a', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)'),
  ('968749eb-718d-5d7b-b874-0e91a0775efc'::uuid, 9, 'Computer Hardware', 'hard', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'About 10 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 50 GB', 'a', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 1,000 GB (decimal)', 'About 100 GB (decimal)', 'About 10,000 GB (decimal)', 'About 1,000,000 GB'),
  ('581d3b3b-d921-5fb6-b673-dfe1f093c7aa'::uuid, 9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which popular design app/website lets students easily create posters, certificates, and invitations using ready templates?', 'Command Prompt', 'Canva', 'Device Manager', 'Disk Cleanup', 'b', 'Which popular design app/website lets students easily create posters, certificates, and invitations using ready templates?', 'Excel', 'Canva', 'Zoom', 'Drive'),
  ('22db0dc7-4f90-5f1f-96b3-71ccc40a6495'::uuid, 9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'What does "Software" mean in simple everyday language?', 'The plastic keyboard keys', 'The power socket on the wall', 'Soft cloth used to clean a monitor', 'The apps, programs, and operating system that run inside a computer or phone', 'd', 'What does "Software" mean in simple everyday language?', 'The power outlets, charging cables and wall sockets that supply electricity to the computer', 'The cloths and cleaning sprays used to remove dust from a computer screen and keyboard', 'The physical keyboard, screen and other computer parts you can hold or touch with your hands', 'The apps, programs, and operating system that run in a computer or phone and tell it what to do'),
  ('d35c5aaf-50f9-5b1a-8187-d02dd78ac17c'::uuid, 9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Which of the following is an Operating System (the core system software that runs a PC or phone)?', 'WhatsApp', 'Canva', 'YouTube', 'Windows 11 / Android', 'd', 'Which of the following is an Operating System (the core system software that runs a PC or phone)?', 'Google Chrome Browser', 'Microsoft Office 365', 'WhatsApp Messenger App', 'Windows 11 / Android'),
  ('3367e013-9ffa-50fc-a321-545bc430ecaf'::uuid, 9, 'Application Software & OS', 'easy', 'Why do schools send circulars and admit cards as a ".pdf" file instead of an editable Word file?', 'PDFs only open at night', 'PDFs automatically translate into 50 languages', 'PDFs do not take even 1 byte of space', 'PDFs keep the exact layout, fonts, and alignment looking identical on every phone and computer', 'd', 'Why do schools send circulars and admit cards as a ".pdf" file instead of an editable Word file?', 'PDF documents can only be opened at night and cannot be viewed during regular school hours', 'PDF documents automatically translate every sentence into fifty languages when they are opened', 'PDF documents occupy no storage space at all, regardless of the number of pages or pictures inside', 'PDFs keep the exact layout, fonts, and alignment looking identical on every phone and computer'),
