  ('4d2a74ff-bc37-56d9-b481-4b6749e7fc31'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only phones with no SIM card', 'Only a computer plugged into it with an HDMI cable', 'Zero — Wi-Fi printers cannot print', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly', 'd', 'If ONE Wi-Fi printer is connected to the school office Wi-Fi router, how many computers on that same Wi-Fi can print to it?', 'Only phones without a SIM card can use the printer over the school''s wireless network', 'Only the computer connected to the printer by an HDMI cable can send documents to it', 'No computer can print at all because printers connected through Wi-Fi cannot receive documents wirelessly', 'All authorized computers/phones on that same Wi-Fi network can share and print to it wirelessly'),
  ('36f02250-b340-54e9-9ddc-c9893d57d1d5'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Disk Formatting', 'Zipping', 'Incognito Browsing', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring', 'd', 'When you mirror your phone or laptop screen wirelessly onto a classroom Smart TV without any cable, what is that feature called?', 'Drive Formatting / Disk Erasing', 'File Compression / Zip Archive', 'Private Browsing / Incognito Mode', 'Screen Casting / Screen Mirroring'),
  ('31c3772c-fce9-5b11-a6a0-a6f8c4db2bec'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'Roll Number', 'IP Address', 'PIN Code', 'Font Size', 'b', 'Every device connected to a network gets an identifying number address (like a house number for delivering data packets). What is it called?', 'Roll Number', 'IP Address', 'PIN Code', 'Font Size'),
  ('2e21baca-c86d-5b1b-a03c-7657084d73f4'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', 'Resolution only affects audio volume', '`4K` uses less data than `480p`', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', 'Both use zero mobile data', 'c', 'You are using a 1.5 GB/day mobile data pack via Hotspot. Watching 2 hours of video at `4K / 2160p` vs `480p` will do what?', '4K and 480p both stream two hours of video without using any mobile data from the internet connection', 'Changing the playback resolution only changes audio volume and has no effect on the amount of video data', '`4K` uses many times more mobile data and can finish your 1.5 GB pack very quickly!', '4K uses less data than 480p because a larger video picture always needs fewer bits to be transmitted'),
  ('48d18620-24c7-552f-8e00-4a546395301c'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It pauses huge background Windows updates so your friend’s mobile data does not drain suddenly', 'It doubles keyboard speed', 'It uninstalls browsers', 'It makes the screen brighter', 'a', 'On a laptop connected to someone’s mobile Hotspot, turning ON "Metered Connection" (or Data Saver) helps because:', 'It can limit large background updates and downloads, helping reduce mobile data use.', 'It permanently doubles keyboard speed whenever the laptop uses a mobile hotspot', 'It uninstalls all browsers automatically so the laptop cannot use the internet connection', 'It increases the brightness of the laptop screen and keeps the display awake for longer'),
  ('66172272-0fd9-5959-93d0-19318cedcea5'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'medium', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', '`5G` Wi-Fi requires a 5G SIM card inside the router', '`2.4G` works only at 2:40 PM', 'There is no difference at all', 'a', 'On modern dual-band home Wi-Fi routers, you often see two Wi-Fi names: `Home_2.4G` and `Home_5G`. What is the practical difference?', '`5 GHz` gives faster speeds nearby in the same room; `2.4 GHz` reaches farther through walls', 'The 5 GHz Wi-Fi network works only if the home router has a 5G mobile SIM card inside', 'The 2.4 GHz wireless network works only when the current time is exactly 2:40 in the afternoon', 'Both networks always have the same speed and range, regardless of walls or distance'),
  ('6ac147db-ebad-5cd5-8282-bd0a717fa645'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Charging another phone from 10 meters away', 'Sending photos or project files fast between two nearby devices wirelessly without wasting internet data', 'Scanning paper books', 'Deleting duplicate contacts', 'b', 'What is "Quick Share / Nearby Share / AirDrop" on modern phones and laptops used for?', 'Sending files to any device worldwide using only its phone number and a satellite connection', 'Sharing photos or files wirelessly between nearby devices, often directly without using mobile data.', 'Digitally scanning paper books and uploading their pages to a printer through a physical USB cable', 'Automatically detecting and deleting duplicate contacts from both devices'' complete address books'),
  ('90faef0c-9e94-567e-8d44-e0fc4766fd2c'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Public Wi-Fi breaks your phone camera', 'Public Wi-Fi deletes SIM contacts', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'Public Wi-Fi drains battery 10x faster', 'c', 'Why should you avoid logging into banking or sensitive accounts on an open, password-free public Wi-Fi at a railway station or café?', 'Public networks automatically copy every photo from a phone''s camera roll to the wireless router', 'Public Wi-Fi immediately damages SIM cards and deletes all contacts stored on a connected phone', 'Unsecured open Wi-Fi networks make it easier for attackers nearby to snoop on traffic or set up fake twin hotspots', 'Public networks use ten times more battery power for every task regardless of signal strength or the type of device'),
  ('21308af1-040e-5dcb-acb0-2d40b0484aff'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'More storage space', 'Higher screen brightness', 'Extra crisp sound quality', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back', 'd', 'In online video calls or multiplayer games, what does "High Ping / High Latency" (e.g., 450 ms instead of 25 ms) feel like?', 'A larger amount of available storage space for saving new files and installing extra games', 'Higher screen brightness while using a phone or a computer for online calls', 'A noticeably clearer and sharper audio signal when speaking or playing with other people online', 'A noticeable delay or lag between clicking/speaking and getting a response back'),
  ('6c9a6519-e87c-56d4-a88a-208dba45cd9c'::uuid, 9, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'Aux Audio Cable', 'VGA Monitor Cable', 'Printer Ribbon', 'Fiber-Optic Cable', 'd', 'What brings ultrahigh-speed broadband into modern schools and homes using hair-thin strands of glass carrying pulses of light?', 'Copper Ethernet cable', 'Wireless radio antenna', 'Coaxial network cable', 'Fiber-Optic Network Cable'),
  ('f9e63492-6746-537f-9a16-9877dbb98a75'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Crop out their name and claim it as yours', 'Forbid anyone else from seeing the source', 'Never use books or references', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself', 'd', 'When you use a diagram, photo, or quote created by someone else in your school presentation, what is the honest thing to do?', 'Remove the creator''s name from the image and present the work as entirely original to your own team', 'Link to a source only when the creator is personally known to you, even when their license requires credit', 'Use the work without credit as long as it is found through a search engine and used in a school project', 'Give clear credit to the original creator or source instead of pretending you made it yourself'),
  ('dc989322-7a29-5594-b542-af4188d53eda'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Open 20 tabs at brightness 20%', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Sit 20 millimeters from the screen for 20 hours', 'Blink only 20 times a day', 'b', 'To keep your eyes comfortable while studying or working on a computer, what does the healthy "20-20-20 Rule" recommend?', 'Every 20 minutes, move the screen 20 cm closer and stare for 20 minutes', 'Every 20 minutes, look at something 20 feet away for 20 seconds to relax your eyes', 'Once every 20 hours, look at a screen from a distance of 20 millimetres for 20 seconds without a break', 'Every 20 minutes, blink exactly 20 times while keeping your eyes fixed on the screen for 20 seconds'),
  ('39fdf96e-4390-5ede-ba2d-d44d6614584f'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'UPI PIN is just your roll number', 'Yes, you must enter UPI PIN to receive gifts', 'NEVER! A UPI PIN is ONLY entered when money is GOING OUT from your account — asking you to enter PIN to "receive" money is a scam!', 'Yes, scanning any QR code automatically credits money after PIN', 'c', 'Important UPI Safety Rule in India: Do you EVER need to enter your secret UPI PIN to RECEIVE money from someone?', 'An incoming UPI transfer needs the recipient''s PIN before the money can reach their account', 'The recipient must share their UPI PIN with the sender to receive an ordinary payment', 'Never enter or share your UPI PIN to receive money; any request to do so is a scam.', 'Receiving a gift requires the recipient to scan a payment request and enter the UPI PIN'),
  ('c497f8d8-3ad7-5e76-8d2c-2acc408029f4'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It slows down typing speed by half', 'It deletes your account after two days', 'It forces two friends to share one account', 'a', 'What is "Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)" on email or social accounts, and why is it great?', 'It adds a second check (like a code on your phone) besides your password, so thieves can’t break in with a leaked password alone', 'It lets anyone with a leaked password receive the second code automatically, without the account owner''s approval', 'It needs two passwords in one box without asking for a second device, code or security key', 'It replaces the password with two public usernames, so knowing the account name alone is enough to sign in from any device online'),
  ('63da6aa4-e84c-5bcc-b134-0e8d69943825'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'There is zero risk', 'a', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'Web browsers permanently block accounts that reuse a password, so there is no chance of unauthorized access', 'A reused password takes extra storage on every device, which is the only security concern to consider', 'An attack on one small game site cannot affect another account, even when the same leaked password is reused across all websites and email services'),
  ('a1a27130-b2ab-5b98-bba0-0ac7804d2857'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'b', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI to produce the complete project, submit its wording unchanged, and claim every idea was independently your own work', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'Use AI during a closed-book test without asking whether its use is allowed and describe all the answers as your own understanding', 'Use AI as a source of final facts because checking dates, quotations and sources is unnecessary when the answer sounds confident, regardless of your teacher''s rules'),
  ('69c7a980-c045-5f8b-a893-193eb2246dcf'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Give it microphone access too', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow everything without reading', 'c', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Allow access to contacts because the camera LED needs phone numbers in order to illuminate a room properly', 'Allow microphone and message access because installing any app guarantees that all its permissions are required', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow all app permissions because it cannot collect or share your contacts or messages without asking you a second time first'),
  ('230fac87-6d46-5f4b-994a-407164b3b602'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'Testing internet speed', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'd', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Software that scans a computer''s storage for viruses and removes any infected files that it happens to find on the device', 'A routine process in which a legitimate company asks every user to post their password publicly for other people to read without any checks or consent', 'A trusted internet service measuring the speed of a connection without asking for private account details or one-time passwords', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs'),
  ('57651b69-077e-5f56-9fb7-c13b150c7fa7'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'd', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The total amount of electrical power used by your computer whenever it accesses the internet', 'The private record of files stored on a device with no activity shared through an online account', 'The physical fingerprints used by a device''s biometric sensor to unlock a phone or laptop', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet'),
  ('48f29c8d-8913-5774-b1ab-f488c458baed'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'b', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Cracked programs are guaranteed to be safer than official versions because they skip all security updates', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Unofficial cracks are automatically scanned, approved and regularly updated by the original software creator before every download from a third-party website', 'Free legal alternatives cannot exist, so downloading a paid application''s crack is the only lawful option'),
  ('ab122a4c-ba38-5526-86b6-7de66538e690'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'c', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click Save and trust that the next person cannot view or reuse a password stored on a shared school computer', 'Click Save but sign out afterwards, because closing the tab always deletes any saved account credentials', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Click Save for this session only, because saved passwords are deleted when another user opens the browser'),
  ('3fb69be9-1006-59ce-8592-796e8eb05362'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'a', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Debate classmates'' personal problems publicly in the group whenever the argument involves someone from class', 'Send unverified reminders and rumours to the whole class first, and confirm them only if a teacher complains', 'Send repeated stickers late at night as long as one useful study message follows'),
  ('29c43738-85d9-5f16-8573-774ee9a0a963'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To slow down your internet', 'To erase your photos', 'a', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Add new visual themes and icon colours even when no security flaws or software problems are being fixed', 'Increase internet download speeds by replacing the Wi-Fi hardware with a faster network chip', 'Remove every personal file so the device can no longer be infected by malicious attachments'),
  ('bbc873ad-3ec8-56f5-a478-acdd08b8756a'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Change their account password', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'b', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Change the password to protect the account, then tell the classmate that the new login details are a surprise', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Read a few recent emails to check whether the account is important, then sign out and tell the classmate afterward', 'Send a harmless message from their account to inform the class, then sign out when the computer is no longer needed'),
  ('008aa3a2-25e1-5e68-8195-4b972076ca07'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Never read what you submit', 'Turn off spell check', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'c', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Submit the generated text without reading it first, provided it is written in complete sentences and looks professional', 'Disable spell check and trust the dates, quotes and book titles whenever the AI describes them in a confident tone', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Include the facts and dates as written, because a confident AI-generated answer never needs an independent source'),
  ('17bf0543-3e49-5bf0-bd68-193c93affec8'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'd', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'A phone can recharge only in silent mode and never charges when notification or alert sounds are on', 'Internet service always costs twice as much after 10 PM, no matter which plan the family has purchased', 'The internal phone clock stops working permanently whenever the user looks at any screen after ten in the evening', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning'),
  ('7269aa1c-d5a9-56b8-9ba2-a335535df22d'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'd', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Send your phone number to the account to settle the argument, then wait for them to decide whether to stop sending messages', 'Reply to the stranger in a private conversation to negotiate directly, then click all of their links so you can decide later whether to report the message', 'Keep the message private, delete the evidence immediately, and avoid telling anyone until the stranger stops contacting you', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher'),
  ('87ba4efb-c872-5345-b0a9-073143a7887d'::uuid, 9, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'b', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Checking your own document for spelling mistakes or comparing it with sources you have already credited', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Using another creator''s work with the necessary permission and giving the creator clear and accurate credit', 'Saving a personal backup copy of your own work to a secure drive and keeping all of the original attribution');
INSERT INTO pg_temp.mtc_revised_seed_20261030 VALUES
  ('46776639-b67f-561c-bb85-12e1ad233982'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Num Lock', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Tab', 'Insert', 'b', 'Which key at the top-left of the keyboard is commonly pressed to cancel a pop-up or exit full-screen video?', 'Ins (Insert)', 'Esc (Escape)', 'Num Lock key', 'Del (Delete)'),
  ('79d7c105-b5c1-55e0-a49d-ec1c715da191'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F1', 'F5', 'F12', 'F2', 'b', 'Which function key is the classic shortcut to REFRESH or reload a webpage in a browser?', 'F1', 'F5', 'F12', 'F2'),
  ('d657fde7-601c-5d58-9d4b-23adb96df49e'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + E', 'a', 'If you pressed Ctrl + Z (Undo) by mistake and want your change back, which shortcut performs REDO?', 'Ctrl + Y', 'Ctrl + R', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + E'),
  ('940e7d95-94fa-5aaf-8688-d29081ea0c1f'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + P', 'Shift + Enter', 'a', 'Which keyboard shortcut lets you quickly switch between open apps/windows on Windows?', 'Alt + Tab', 'Ctrl + C', 'Ctrl + P', 'Shift + Enter'),
  ('2d8af443-60c6-5951-bb51-ce5b805adc0e'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'Tab', 'Alt', 'Ctrl', 'a', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'Enter', 'AltGr', 'Space'),
  ('95cb950f-258d-5d5b-9519-50b390404091'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N', 'd', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N'),
  ('783b39d7-e35d-5a40-b3ee-8a27ec640cf1'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Translates the page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Closes the browser', 'a', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'Translates the current page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi access', 'Closes the current browser tab'),
  ('dc59bbf6-8c4e-5d01-84d4-93ab9fab4934'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the screen white', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'b', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Turns the browser screen white', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens the Microsoft Word app', 'Saves bookmarks in this tab'),
  ('20f106bf-d366-5ada-ac00-6fdbf9dec36e'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause/Break', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'Page Down', 'b', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'Pause or Break key', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'ScrLk (Scroll Lock key)', 'PgDn (Page Down key)'),
  ('bc8f7bbb-48c9-501c-802e-f4acde1292f5'::uuid, 10, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F1', 'F4', 'F8', 'F2', 'd', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F1', 'F4', 'F8', 'F2'),
