  ('979dfa62-2d18-57e0-b0e7-3cd360959942'::uuid, 10, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Your internet speed test shows `100 Mbps` (Megabits per second). Since 8 bits = 1 Byte, roughly how many Megabytes (`MB`) can download in 1 second?', '0.1 MB per second', '100 GB per second', 'Exactly 800 MB per second', 'Around 12.5 MB per second (`100 ÷ 8`)', 'd', 'Your internet speed test shows `100 Mbps` (Megabits per second). Since 8 bits = 1 Byte, roughly how many Megabytes (`MB`) can download in 1 second?', 'About 100 MB per second (100 x 1)', 'About 800 MB per second (100 x 8)', 'About 0.1 MB per second (100 divided by 1,000)', 'Around 12.5 MB per second (`100 ÷ 8`)'),
  ('d50ec850-3209-5771-ac3a-b57575e16ce5'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'There is zero risk', 'It uses extra storage on your phone', 'Browsers block repeated passwords', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!', 'd', 'Why is reusing the EXACT SAME password across 10 different games, websites, and your main email risky?', 'An attack on one small game site cannot affect another account, even when the same leaked password is reused across all websites and email services', 'A reused password takes extra storage on every device, which is the only security concern to consider', 'Web browsers permanently block accounts that reuse a password, so there is no chance of unauthorized access', 'If even one small game site gets hacked, attackers immediately try that same password on your email and other accounts!'),
  ('ade364bd-d13b-5984-8da1-fb8ca236cc98'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Copy-paste the entire AI output without reading a word and sign it as 100% your own', 'Trust every single date or quote from AI without checking', 'Use AI during closed-book tests', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped', 'd', 'How should a responsible student use AI tools (like ChatGPT or Gemini) when working on a project or assignment?', 'Use AI to produce the complete project, submit its wording unchanged, and claim every idea was independently your own work', 'Use AI as a source of final facts because checking dates, quotations and sources is unnecessary when the answer sounds confident, regardless of your teacher''s rules', 'Use AI during a closed-book test without asking whether its use is allowed and describe all the answers as your own understanding', 'Use AI to brainstorm, understand tough ideas, or debug — then write/build in your own understanding and honestly mention where AI helped'),
  ('e7cb6534-ae46-5987-8f84-8f32e9214432'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Flashlights need your contacts to shine brighter', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow everything without reading', 'Give it microphone access too', 'b', 'You install a simple "Flashlight" app on a phone, and it suddenly asks permission to read your Contacts, Call Logs, and Messages. What should you think?', 'Allow access to contacts because the camera LED needs phone numbers in order to illuminate a room properly', 'Deny/uninstall! A flashlight only needs the camera LED — asking for private contacts and messages is a big privacy red flag', 'Allow all app permissions because it cannot collect or share your contacts or messages without asking you a second time first', 'Allow microphone and message access because installing any app guarantees that all its permissions are required'),
  ('14f82daa-4a7e-59a2-b1b3-dc18e9fb3b80'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Cleaning computer fans', 'Searching for ocean documentaries online', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'Testing internet speed', 'c', 'What is "Phishing"?', 'Software that scans a computer''s storage for viruses and removes any infected files that it happens to find on the device', 'A trusted internet service measuring the speed of a connection without asking for private account details or one-time passwords', 'Fake emails, SMS, or look-alike websites pretending to be a trusted bank/company to trick you into typing passwords or OTPs', 'A routine process in which a legitimate company asks every user to post their password publicly for other people to read without any checks or consent'),
  ('f0f8f8a7-3fa4-53ab-a319-25e1b3473672'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'a', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The private record of files stored on a device with no activity shared through an online account', 'The physical fingerprints used by a device''s biometric sensor to unlock a phone or laptop', 'The total amount of electrical power used by your computer whenever it accesses the internet'),
  ('a410ea4e-8329-58b7-a37e-be1a90d70fcd'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'a', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'Unofficial cracks are automatically scanned, approved and regularly updated by the original software creator before every download from a third-party website', 'Cracked programs are guaranteed to be safer than official versions because they skip all security updates', 'Free legal alternatives cannot exist, so downloading a paid application''s crack is the only lawful option'),
  ('4bd6ccad-b932-51b5-8653-83f5b096acc5'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'b', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click Save but sign out afterwards, because closing the tab always deletes any saved account credentials', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'Click Save and trust that the next person cannot view or reuse a password stored on a shared school computer', 'Click Save for this session only, because saved passwords are deleted when another user opens the browser'),
  ('ed6d8a84-ae24-5c44-915e-91f709c91b26'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'c', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Debate classmates'' personal problems publicly in the group whenever the argument involves someone from class', 'Send unverified reminders and rumours to the whole class first, and confirm them only if a teacher complains', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Send repeated stickers late at night as long as one useful study message follows'),
  ('b66a76a7-bf99-5e97-af93-380fe36db1ea'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To erase your photos', 'To slow down your internet', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'd', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Remove every personal file so the device can no longer be infected by malicious attachments', 'Increase internet download speeds by replacing the Wi-Fi hardware with a faster network chip', 'Add new visual themes and icon colours even when no security flaws or software problems are being fixed', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them'),
  ('69d801ce-045e-572a-95fe-dc73257c409e'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'd', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Change the password to protect the account, then tell the classmate that the new login details are a surprise', 'Send a harmless message from their account to inform the class, then sign out when the computer is no longer needed', 'Read a few recent emails to check whether the account is important, then sign out and tell the classmate afterward', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time'),
  ('332d64a5-1e1c-5ce9-9d78-09777bf850b8'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Never read what you submit', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Turn off spell check', 'b', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Submit the generated text without reading it first, provided it is written in complete sentences and looks professional', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Include the facts and dates as written, because a confident AI-generated answer never needs an independent source', 'Disable spell check and trust the dates, quotes and book titles whenever the AI describes them in a confident tone'),
  ('00b65885-6751-567f-8c19-b5fee9a07275'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'c', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'A phone can recharge only in silent mode and never charges when notification or alert sounds are on', 'The internal phone clock stops working permanently whenever the user looks at any screen after ten in the evening', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'Internet service always costs twice as much after 10 PM, no matter which plan the family has purchased'),
  ('64430da1-a233-5410-a70c-d015adeb7094'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'a', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Reply to the stranger in a private conversation to negotiate directly, then click all of their links so you can decide later whether to report the message', 'Keep the message private, delete the evidence immediately, and avoid telling anyone until the stranger stops contacting you', 'Send your phone number to the account to settle the argument, then wait for them to decide whether to stop sending messages'),
  ('9eff5e05-d40b-5e08-b366-d5ed217a7ba0'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'a', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'Using another creator''s work with the necessary permission and giving the creator clear and accurate credit', 'Checking your own document for spelling mistakes or comparing it with sources you have already credited', 'Saving a personal backup copy of your own work to a secure drive and keeping all of the original attribution'),
  ('82d68c62-b53a-5a32-bce3-101c93a29f85'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'b', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Keep the monitor below knee height and bend the neck downward continuously while leaning very close toward the keyboard and desk', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Sit with a twisted back, one leg tucked under the chair, and the screen turned far to one side', 'Bring the face very close to the keyboard and keep the elbows raised without supporting the forearms'),
  ('c55faf51-a203-58d2-a85e-cfc51980620f'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '108', '139', '1930', '101', 'c', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '1098', '1810', '1930', '1091'),
  ('63ecaa81-4863-58be-a415-4cc726965d46'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'd', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'A backup copy stored in a deeply nested folder with the original video and voice completely unchanged', 'An encrypted video that remains unchanged but requires a special key before any authorised viewer can open it', 'A high-resolution recording of an actual underwater scene that has not been altered with artificial intelligence at all', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did'),
  ('9eab1f8f-bda7-5ba5-b088-e8de88b5bee7'::uuid, 10, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'd', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Transfer the money immediately to the unfamiliar number, then call the family member on their known phone to check the request', 'Share the family''s banking OTPs with the caller so that they can prove that the request is legitimate', 'Install the caller''s suggested screen-sharing app before verifying who is asking for the money', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!');
INSERT INTO pg_temp.mtc_revised_seed_20261030 VALUES
  ('0ee888b5-1547-51f0-a33a-ae606dd67707'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'Alt', 'Ctrl', 'Tab', 'a', 'To type a single capital letter or the "@" symbol above the number 2 without turning on Caps Lock, which key do you hold?', 'Shift', 'AltGr', 'Space', 'Enter'),
  ('eb572541-ecd4-5115-8332-df3cc7406d0d'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + M', 'c', 'Which shortcut opens a brand-new blank document or window in most apps?', 'Ctrl + D', 'Ctrl + B', 'Ctrl + N', 'Ctrl + M'),
  ('7cddccd9-d891-517d-a3bd-d0ddc9a5a6a0'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Closes the browser', 'Translates the page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi', 'Opens a new browser tab', 'd', 'In a web browser like Chrome or Edge, what does pressing Ctrl + T do?', 'Closes the current browser tab', 'Translates the current page', 'Turns off Wi-Fi access', 'Opens a new browser tab'),
  ('1e4834be-b7c6-55a7-9935-bf7fdee11ac9'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens Microsoft Word', 'Turns the screen white', 'Saves all bookmarks', 'a', 'In a web browser, what does pressing Ctrl + W do?', 'Closes only the current tab', 'Opens the Microsoft Word app', 'Turns the browser screen white', 'Saves bookmarks in this tab'),
  ('d09aa490-01b2-54bc-868e-22c062370df7'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Scroll Lock', 'Pause/Break', 'Page Down', 'a', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'ScrLk (Scroll Lock key)', 'Pause or Break key', 'PgDn (Page Down key)'),
  ('680bb177-637d-509b-8426-fe4eaf98340d'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1', 'F2', 'd', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F8', 'F1', 'F2'),
  ('22a7e852-3bb7-5ffe-944a-6291b349310a'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'Increases speaker volume', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four new folders', 'c', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Enables Bluetooth on the current PC', 'Increases the volume of the current app', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four folders in the current application'),
  ('e046424f-d12d-5895-b724-6a7e9374682b'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Increases internet speed', 'Opens calculator', 'Adds a new user account', 'a', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'Increases the speed of the internet connection', 'Opens the calculator beside the current webpage', 'Creates a new account for the current web browser user'),
  ('82057334-64b3-5aa0-af76-790056d6fb5b'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Closes all tabs', 'c', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Turns off sound for every open application', 'Clears all the pages that are stored in browser history', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Resets the zoom level for every browser tab'),
  ('18f6d541-1fb7-54fb-b6bf-fe9ffe9946ad'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Closes the browser tab', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Erases what you typed', 'b', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Moves the cursor to the previous input box', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form and sends every answer to the server', 'Clears the answer from the currently active input box'),
  ('20ef623b-51f6-5374-a8f4-a02afd86f82b'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Windows Key + L', 'Ctrl + L', 'Alt + L', 'Windows Key + O', 'a', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Windows Key + L', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + M', 'Windows Key + R'),
  ('4dffec02-fb3e-58b2-9589-3c17d2fdaba7'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Ctrl + D', 'Alt + D', 'a', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + R', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + L'),
  ('5e2a4570-1271-5ea5-9f9a-732832a1545d'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Alt + Z', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'Alt + Home', 'Shift + F5', 'b', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Shift + W', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'Ctrl + Shift + N', 'Ctrl + Shift + H'),
  ('1416f0f5-64c1-53ab-9774-f8615498b920'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the file to Desktop', 'Nothing happens', 'It copies the file twice', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'd', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the selected file to Desktop without placing it in the Recycle Bin', 'It moves the file to the Recycle Bin where it can be restored later', 'It deletes the shortcut but keeps the actual file unchanged on the same drive', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin'),
  ('d607f730-16c7-52ab-9a39-17d43b613539'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Alt + E', 'Ctrl + E', 'Windows Key + F', 'Windows Key + E', 'd', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + R', 'Windows Key + E'),
  ('7b899582-e8a9-5b0c-aca6-153acb4294d8'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once', 'The entire document', 'Only punctuation marks', 'Only one single letter', 'a', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once', 'The entire document regardless of where the cursor is', 'The entire line to the left of the cursor at once', 'The entire word to the right of the current cursor position at once'),
  ('25271dc4-68d0-5387-ae78-1605a6524a2e'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F11', 'F3', 'F7', 'F1', 'a', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F11', 'F12', 'F13', 'F10'),
  ('dc97b942-0ec4-5ed9-ac51-219d23e26db4'::uuid, 11, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Windows Key + M', 'Ctrl + Alt + P', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Shift + Tab', 'c', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Ctrl + Shift + F11', 'Ctrl + Shift + Tab', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Ctrl + Shift + F12'),
  ('711f358a-5bea-5dcf-a2b1-2486e81c8c32'::uuid, 11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To boost Wi-Fi signal', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To blow dust onto the screen', 'To make music louder', 'b', 'What is the main job of the small spinning fan inside a laptop or desktop cabinet?', 'To increase the processor''s computing performance by supplying it with extra electrical current', 'To keep the processor and internal parts cool so the computer does not overheat', 'To remove dust from the laptop without changing its internal temperature', 'To supply battery power by turning the spinning fan into electrical current'),
  ('2c9cb0bf-100f-5fa2-a3c4-98a30cd18ab0'::uuid, 11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'Both are names for the screen', 'RAM is only for printers', 'RAM stores photos forever; Storage deletes everything on restart', 'a', 'In everyday phones and computers, what is the simple difference between RAM and Storage (SSD/ROM)?', 'RAM holds active apps temporarily while working; Storage keeps your photos and files saved even when powered off', 'RAM stores files permanently when powered off; Storage holds open apps only until the computer is shut down', 'RAM and Storage both refer to the screen, and neither has any role in keeping data or running applications', 'RAM is found only in printers and holds photos forever; Storage erases all of its contents after every restart'),
  ('f4e00f14-0660-5af4-ad04-bec6ea799c71'::uuid, 11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'A bigger mouse pad', 'RAM (working memory)', 'A louder speaker', 'A longer power cable', 'b', 'If your computer opens 15 browser tabs and starts feeling sluggish when switching apps, having more of which part helps most?', 'Internal SSD drive', 'RAM (working memory)', 'Wi-Fi network modem', 'Graphics processor'),
  ('64e54f4c-a5d1-5848-8244-715a24a56765'::uuid, 11, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'The screen becomes wider', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'It prints paper automatically', 'You never need to charge the battery', 'b', 'Modern laptops use an SSD instead of an older spinning Hard Disk (HDD). What everyday benefit do you notice right away?', 'It removes the need for backups because an SSD can never fail or lose data', 'The laptop boots up and opens apps much faster, with no moving disk parts', 'It automatically increases available RAM for every app without changing any memory modules in the laptop', 'It improves Wi-Fi coverage even if all the wireless network hardware remains completely unchanged'),
