  ('3f09eb1d-d0ff-57fe-aaea-a425ccabf238'::uuid, 11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'What is the role of a "Firewall" in Windows or a school router?', 'It prevents physical fire in the computer room', 'It monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic and blocks unauthorized outside connections', 'It deletes old browser bookmarks', 'It heats up the CPU in winter', 'b', 'What is the role of a "Firewall" in Windows or a school router?', 'It prevents physical fires by cutting power to the whole building whenever network traffic increases', 'It monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic and blocks unauthorized outside connections', 'It searches local storage and deletes every malicious file without checking network connections at all', 'It assigns web addresses to every website on the internet and stores them permanently on your computer'),
  ('94bb70fb-45aa-5f78-907d-49222c7bee9c'::uuid, 11, 'Basic Networking & Connectivity', 'hard', 'Why should you change the default admin login (`admin / admin`) printed on the bottom sticker of a new home Wi-Fi router?', 'Default passwords use more electricity', 'It voids the monitor warranty', 'Anyone connected nearby who knows common default logins could open router settings and change your Wi-Fi or DNS!', 'Otherwise Wi-Fi turns off after 24 hours', 'c', 'Why should you change the default admin login (`admin / admin`) printed on the bottom sticker of a new home Wi-Fi router?', 'Changing the router login makes every connected computer immune to all malware and viruses on the internet forever', 'The default login increases electricity use and makes the router''s power supply consume extra current', 'Anyone connected nearby who knows common default logins could open router settings and change your Wi-Fi or DNS!', 'The manufacturer''s default login disables internet access after twenty-four hours unless it is changed'),
  ('1ec176f2-67a1-5e0d-a2a0-88dceebddb19'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'A fingerprint unlock sensor', 'The size of your laptop in inches', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'Walking barefoot in the computer lab', 'c', 'What does your "Digital Footprint" mean?', 'The private record of files stored on a device with no activity shared through an online account', 'The physical fingerprints used by a device''s biometric sensor to unlock a phone or laptop', 'The lasting trail of posts, comments, photos, and public activity associated with you on the internet', 'The total amount of electrical power used by your computer whenever it accesses the internet'),
  ('8f45734d-7bb2-5e44-93ed-efd3d9d3fa76'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Official free alternatives like VLC, GIMP, or LibreOffice do not exist', 'It upgrades your monitor', 'Cracked software runs faster and safer than official apps', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!', 'd', 'Why is downloading "Cracked / Pirated" paid software or game cheats from shady websites dangerous as well as unethical?', 'Free legal alternatives cannot exist, so downloading a paid application''s crack is the only lawful option', 'Cracked programs are guaranteed to be safer than official versions because they skip all security updates', 'Unofficial cracks are automatically scanned, approved and regularly updated by the original software creator before every download from a third-party website', 'Besides disrespecting creators’ work, pirated cracks are one of the #1 ways password-stealing malware infects home PCs!'),
  ('75b53ca9-ed5b-5587-a6db-97b56d522bfc'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click "Save" so you never have to type again', 'Write your password on a sticky note on the monitor', 'Share it with the café owner', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!', 'd', 'Before clicking "Save Password" when Chrome asks on a shared school or cyber-café computer, what should you ALWAYS choose?', 'Click Save but sign out afterwards, because closing the tab always deletes any saved account credentials', 'Click Save for this session only, because saved passwords are deleted when another user opens the browser', 'Click Save and trust that the next person cannot view or reuse a password stored on a shared school computer', 'Click "Never" — saving your password on a shared computer lets the next person log straight into your account!'),
  ('578ce39e-7e73-51e7-9116-075b9c339db2'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Starting personal arguments in front of 60 people', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Sending 80 stickers in a row at midnight', 'Forwarding unverified rumors', 'b', 'In a class study WhatsApp/Telegram group, what keeps the group helpful and respectful for everyone?', 'Debate classmates'' personal problems publicly in the group whenever the argument involves someone from class', 'Keeping messages relevant, polite, avoiding late-night spam chains, and respecting classmates’ opinions', 'Send repeated stickers late at night as long as one useful study message follows', 'Send unverified reminders and rumours to the whole class first, and confirm them only if a teacher complains'),
  ('34d7b184-bf1c-589c-98bc-7e8a7786b448'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'To erase your photos', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'To slow down your internet', 'c', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Remove every personal file so the device can no longer be infected by malicious attachments', 'Add new visual themes and icon colours even when no security flaws or software problems are being fixed', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Increase internet download speeds by replacing the Wi-Fi hardware with a faster network chip'),
  ('4d379a20-b995-5a45-b003-acb18c00719b'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'a', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Send a harmless message from their account to inform the class, then sign out when the computer is no longer needed', 'Read a few recent emails to check whether the account is important, then sign out and tell the classmate afterward', 'Change the password to protect the account, then tell the classmate that the new login details are a surprise'),
  ('7249d8ba-0305-5415-9811-edc441a38cf0'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Never read what you submit', 'Turn off spell check', 'a', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'Include the facts and dates as written, because a confident AI-generated answer never needs an independent source', 'Submit the generated text without reading it first, provided it is written in complete sentences and looks professional', 'Disable spell check and trust the dates, quotes and book titles whenever the AI describes them in a confident tone'),
  ('705cf6f2-2106-5c9e-97c9-ad3e8424a52e'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'b', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'The internal phone clock stops working permanently whenever the user looks at any screen after ten in the evening', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'A phone can recharge only in silent mode and never charges when notification or alert sounds are on', 'Internet service always costs twice as much after 10 PM, no matter which plan the family has purchased'),
  ('dc77f710-879c-50d9-9ab0-336452e55ced'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Click every link they sent', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'c', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Reply to the stranger in a private conversation to negotiate directly, then click all of their links so you can decide later whether to report the message', 'Keep the message private, delete the evidence immediately, and avoid telling anyone until the stranger stops contacting you', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send your phone number to the account to settle the argument, then wait for them to decide whether to stop sending messages'),
  ('c40096d3-e5dc-5f01-9b14-480a63651c52'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Checking spelling in Word', 'Using open-source software legally', 'Saving a backup copy on a pendrive', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit', 'd', 'What is "Plagiarism" in school projects and digital work?', 'Saving a personal backup copy of your own work to a secure drive and keeping all of the original attribution', 'Checking your own document for spelling mistakes or comparing it with sources you have already credited', 'Using another creator''s work with the necessary permission and giving the creator clear and accurate credit', 'Copying someone else’s article, code, or artwork and presenting it as your own original work without credit'),
  ('ed64a110-c00b-50b0-b2aa-a6637cf24287'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'd', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Keep the monitor below knee height and bend the neck downward continuously while leaning very close toward the keyboard and desk', 'Bring the face very close to the keyboard and keep the elbows raised without supporting the forearms', 'Sit with a twisted back, one leg tucked under the chair, and the screen turned far to one side', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low'),
  ('dee3d7c8-a161-5f38-ad73-6f21d0f8fac2'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '108', '1930', '101', '139', 'b', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '1098', '1930', '1091', '1810'),
  ('b7f4967f-fcd7-51c9-8b97-340bc720f7f9'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'c', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'A backup copy stored in a deeply nested folder with the original video and voice completely unchanged', 'A high-resolution recording of an actual underwater scene that has not been altered with artificial intelligence at all', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'An encrypted video that remains unchanged but requires a special key before any authorised viewer can open it'),
  ('b7545891-c136-53ef-a94a-be8168736413'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'a', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Share the family''s banking OTPs with the caller so that they can prove that the request is legitimate', 'Install the caller''s suggested screen-sharing app before verifying who is asking for the money', 'Transfer the money immediately to the unfamiliar number, then call the family member on their known phone to check the request'),
  ('300a314e-edc0-569b-baf5-7422424e7d9c'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!', 'To clean dust from your phone speaker', 'To double your mobile battery life', 'Banks require AnyDesk for every account', 'a', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!', 'A shared screen prevents the other person from seeing notifications, banking apps and one-time passcodes', 'The app gives the caller no control or information and guarantees that your banking activity remains private', 'A caller can verify your identity safely only by controlling your device, even when you did not initiate the call'),
  ('ade9e244-903d-5ddf-8211-2a13f88c21ee'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Parents’ bank account numbers and Aadhaar passwords', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!', 'Personal email passwords', 'Home Wi-Fi passwords of every student', 'b', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Collect parents'' bank account details, private identity credentials and financial information even though the club does not need it', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!', 'Collect the password for each student''s personal email account to simplify future club announcements', 'Collect every student''s home Wi-Fi password so the club can access the family''s router whenever necessary'),
  ('883bc0ab-4005-585b-b71b-e68b8ba4296e'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'Nobody is allowed to view the image', 'You can sell it as your own painting without credit', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The file contains a virus', 'c', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'The license prevents anyone from viewing the work, even if the creator has posted it on a public webpage', 'The license allows you to claim that you created the work and remove any required credits from the finished video', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The license automatically makes every work public domain and allows all personal and commercial uses without any restrictions or attribution whatsoever'),
  ('2169b7fd-7e23-5965-81ac-c33e445f1039'::uuid, 11, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break screens with a hammer in class', 'Throw batteries into rivers', 'Burn plastic circuit boards in the backyard', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water', 'd', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break the screens into smaller pieces in the classroom and mix all of the sharp fragments with ordinary school waste', 'Throw old batteries into a river or drain and assume that the water will safely dissolve their contents', 'Burn the plastic circuit boards and cable coverings outdoors so that the remaining metal can be stored at home', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water');
INSERT INTO pg_temp.mtc_revised_seed_20261030 VALUES
  ('59095c04-6508-5c95-b311-26bdbf3ba7df'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'Page Down', 'Pause/Break', 'Scroll Lock', 'a', 'Which key on a Windows keyboard is used to capture a screenshot of your entire screen?', 'PrtSc (Print Screen)', 'PgDn (Page Down key)', 'Pause or Break key', 'ScrLk (Scroll Lock key)'),
  ('c436f0cf-53ad-5053-b306-ec1e2fae0b4e'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F1', 'F2', 'F8', 'c', 'When a file or folder is selected on Windows, pressing which function key lets you RENAME it immediately?', 'F4', 'F1', 'F2', 'F8'),
  ('e24c56a1-1938-5758-b653-c6ec1c9cbbd9'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Turns on Bluetooth', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four new folders', 'Increases speaker volume', 'b', 'What does pressing Alt + F4 do on a Windows computer?', 'Enables Bluetooth on the current PC', 'Closes the currently active app or window', 'Opens four folders in the current application', 'Increases the volume of the current app'),
  ('539351b2-682c-544a-8c44-8cf964e37c17'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Adds a new user account', 'Increases internet speed', 'Opens calculator', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger', 'd', 'In a browser, pressing Ctrl and the "+" (plus) key together does what?', 'Creates a new account for the current web browser user', 'Increases the speed of the internet connection', 'Opens the calculator beside the current webpage', 'Zooms in to make text and images appear larger'),
  ('dbb55d4b-50eb-5e8a-a06c-e4805a79e8b0'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Deletes the webpage', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Mutes computer sound', 'Closes all tabs', 'b', 'After zooming in on a webpage, pressing Ctrl + 0 (zero) does what?', 'Clears all the pages that are stored in browser history', 'Resets the page zoom back to normal (100%)', 'Turns off sound for every open application', 'Resets the zoom level for every browser tab'),
  ('eea62554-ce2d-53f5-a9df-ec3a50f09405'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form immediately', 'Closes the browser tab', 'Erases what you typed', 'a', 'When filling out an online form (like Name, Roll No, Class), pressing the Tab key usually does what?', 'Moves the cursor neatly to the next input box', 'Submits the form and sends every answer to the server', 'Moves the cursor to the previous input box', 'Clears the answer from the currently active input box'),
  ('ccc02ae0-d4ae-57b4-a435-9885819f14cd'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'easy', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Ctrl + L', 'Alt + L', 'Windows Key + L', 'Windows Key + O', 'c', 'If you step away from a computer for a minute, which Windows shortcut immediately LOCKS your screen?', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + M', 'Windows Key + L', 'Windows Key + R'),
  ('f9d677a2-dcc8-5045-9c0f-8740d1aed132'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Alt + D', 'Ctrl + D', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + D', 'd', 'Which Windows shortcut minimizes all open windows at once so you can see the Desktop?', 'Windows Key + L', 'Windows Key + P', 'Windows Key + R', 'Windows Key + D'),
  ('65296de1-bd5e-5f1a-9a5d-0ccb35659409'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Alt + Z', 'Shift + F5', 'Alt + Home', 'Ctrl + Shift + T', 'd', 'You accidentally closed an important tab in Chrome/Edge! Which lifesaver shortcut reopens the last closed tab?', 'Ctrl + Shift + W', 'Ctrl + Shift + H', 'Ctrl + Shift + N', 'Ctrl + Shift + T'),
  ('edcf92b2-d4f5-55d1-9404-47ff7759cca6'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the file to Desktop', 'It copies the file twice', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'Nothing happens', 'c', 'What happens when you delete a file using Shift + Delete instead of just pressing Delete?', 'It moves the selected file to Desktop without placing it in the Recycle Bin', 'It deletes the shortcut but keeps the actual file unchanged on the same drive', 'It permanently deletes the file without sending it to the Recycle Bin', 'It moves the file to the Recycle Bin where it can be restored later'),
  ('cf60dce7-3496-5ff1-9578-ce6da7ac62d8'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Alt + E', 'Windows Key + F', 'Windows Key + E', 'Ctrl + E', 'c', 'Which Windows shortcut opens File Explorer ("This PC" / Folders) directly?', 'Windows Key + D', 'Windows Key + R', 'Windows Key + E', 'Windows Key + P'),
  ('d69b94e4-f0a9-541c-b603-fbee552891d8'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'Only one single letter', 'The entire document', 'Only punctuation marks', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once', 'd', 'While typing a sentence, holding Ctrl and pressing Backspace (Ctrl + Backspace) erases what?', 'The entire word to the right of the current cursor position at once', 'The entire document regardless of where the cursor is', 'The entire line to the left of the cursor at once', 'The entire word to the left of the cursor at once'),
  ('f8c44c89-7a70-575b-8511-baffdd90c501'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F3', 'F7', 'F11', 'F1', 'c', 'Which function key toggles Full-Screen mode ON or OFF in almost all web browsers?', 'F12', 'F13', 'F11', 'F10'),
  ('08cfb609-770f-5bfa-b8c0-4f5e4730cffb'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'medium', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Ctrl + Alt + P', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Windows Key + M', 'Shift + Tab', 'b', 'If a program freezes on Windows, which direct shortcut opens Task Manager immediately?', 'Ctrl + Shift + Tab', 'Ctrl + Shift + Esc', 'Ctrl + Shift + F11', 'Ctrl + Shift + F12'),
  ('0327f962-e32f-56bf-ace9-b9510c57dfb4'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'Which modern Windows shortcut lets you drag and capture a screenshot of just ONE selected area of your screen?', 'Alt + S', 'Ctrl + F4', 'Windows Key + Shift + S', 'Ctrl + P', 'c', 'Which modern Windows shortcut lets you drag and capture a screenshot of just ONE selected area of your screen?', 'Windows Key + Shift + E', 'Windows Key + Shift + P', 'Windows Key + Shift + S', 'Windows Key + Shift + D'),
  ('ed1189d3-9ae8-5af9-8fc2-2a5c03db3b61'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In Word, Google Docs, or Notepad, which shortcut opens "Find and Replace" to swap a repeated word across the whole file?', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + J', 'Ctrl + H', 'd', 'In Word, Google Docs, or Notepad, which shortcut opens "Find and Replace" to swap a repeated word across the whole file?', 'Ctrl + M', 'Ctrl + W', 'Ctrl + J', 'Ctrl + H'),
  ('ea0429e6-027a-53b7-abd7-fb4dd2a08c04'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In a web browser, pressing Ctrl + L (or Alt + D) quickly highlights what?', 'The top Address / URL bar so you can type a website or search immediately', 'Your computer wallpaper', 'The Recycle Bin', 'The bottom footer of the webpage', 'a', 'In a web browser, pressing Ctrl + L (or Alt + D) quickly highlights what?', 'The top Address / URL bar so you can type a website or search immediately', 'The desktop background shown behind the currently open windows and applications', 'The Downloads panel showing all the files you have recently saved from the internet', 'The footer of the page, where its links and contact details are displayed'),
  ('731f3741-49c2-5459-9e7e-681f78cc0eac'::uuid, 12, 'Keyboard Shortcuts', 'hard', 'In Word, Google Docs, or email apps, pressing Ctrl + K on selected text lets you insert what?', 'An audio recording', 'A clickable hyperlink (website link)', 'A page break', 'A password lock', 'b', 'In Word, Google Docs, or email apps, pressing Ctrl + K on selected text lets you insert what?', 'An audio clip beside the selected text', 'A clickable hyperlink (website link)', 'A page break after the selected text', 'A password to lock the current document'),
  ('54ca0f39-3700-5ad9-bd4b-19d23256ab4d'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'PS/2 round port', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'VGA port', 'CD-ROM slot', 'b', 'Which newer oval-shaped reversible charging/data port is found on almost all modern Android phones and newer laptops?', 'Optical CD-ROM slot', 'USB Type-C (USB-C)', 'VGA display port', 'PS/2 keyboard port'),
  ('012d57b9-e8db-5d2e-ad1f-936050543a1f'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Dashboard', 'Motherboard', 'Whiteboard', 'Clipboard', 'b', 'What do we call the main circuit board inside a computer that connects the processor, RAM, storage, and ports together?', 'Graphics card', 'Motherboard', 'Cooling fan', 'Memory card'),
  ('f691dfc2-7d62-5915-8e8b-f2d5379f0c2f'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Reinstall Windows immediately', 'Buy a new monitor', 'Delete your files', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF', 'd', 'If a wireless mouse stops moving the cursor on screen, what is the FIRST simple hardware thing you should check?', 'Reinstall Windows first because the mouse battery cannot affect movement of the screen pointer', 'Replace the monitor first because the pointer is always controlled by the display hardware', 'Delete files because a full disk means the mouse cannot work at all in any app', 'Check if its battery is low or its tiny power switch underneath is turned OFF'),
  ('ccc082f3-f3aa-5c07-9b51-f40961e79b97'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Laser printer', 'Router antenna', 'Thumb drive', 'a', 'A pen-like tool used by digital artists and students to write or draw neatly on a tablet screen is called a:', 'Stylus', 'Mouse', 'Trackpad', 'Joystick'),
  ('305c9617-ae49-5bb2-9dd8-277be203245f'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)', 'b', 'Which storage capacity is LARGER when comparing a pendrive or laptop storage?', '1 Gigabyte (1 GB)', '1 Terabyte (1 TB)', '1 Kilobyte (1 KB)', '1 Megabyte (1 MB)'),
  ('fe32fd86-f850-59cf-a797-f5ead56ff0ae'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 50 GB', 'About 2 GB', 'About 10 GB', 'About 1,000 GB (1,024 GB)', 'd', 'Roughly how many Gigabytes (GB) make 1 Terabyte (TB) on a hard drive?', 'About 1,000,000 GB', 'About 10,000 GB (decimal)', 'About 100 GB (decimal)', 'About 1,000 GB (decimal)'),
  ('ffdce8d2-efc2-5d36-9dd2-6f7073157086'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'easy', 'Before pulling out a USB pendrive while files are copying, why should you wait or click "Eject"?', 'The keyboard will lock', 'It uses up Wi-Fi data', 'Pulling it out mid-write can corrupt or damage the files being saved', 'Otherwise the monitor turns black forever', 'c', 'Before pulling out a USB pendrive while files are copying, why should you wait or click "Eject"?', 'Removing it during a copy changes all file types into formats that no program can read', 'Removing it during a copy erases every existing file on the computer''s internal drive', 'Pulling it out mid-write can corrupt or damage the files being saved', 'Removing it mid-copy can permanently damage the USB port on the computer'),
  ('de4ff315-1814-5294-89dd-b8fab22976dd'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Which computer component is specially helpful for smooth 3D video editing, animation, and modern games?', 'Floppy drive', 'Ink cartridge', 'RJ45 plug', 'GPU (Graphics Card / Graphics Processor)', 'd', 'Which computer component is specially helpful for smooth 3D video editing, animation, and modern games?', 'Removable floppy disk drive for data storage', 'Replacement ink cartridge for a desktop printer', 'Wired RJ45 connector for a computer network cable', 'GPU (Graphics Processing Unit / Graphics Card)'),
  ('66d671ce-b041-5e18-9935-76b1eb82fe4a'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'Why should you NEVER block the air vents on the bottom of a laptop by placing it deep into a thick blanket for hours?', 'It deletes browser bookmarks', 'It makes the screen brightness drop to zero', 'Blocked vents trap heat inside, causing overheating, slow performance, and battery wear', 'It disconnects Bluetooth earbuds', 'c', 'Why should you NEVER block the air vents on the bottom of a laptop by placing it deep into a thick blanket for hours?', 'Trapped air weakens wireless signals so the laptop loses Wi-Fi whenever it is placed near fabric', 'Blocked openings force the screen brightness to drop to zero and permanently damage the display', 'Blocked vents trap heat inside, causing overheating, slow performance, and battery wear', 'Covered vents prevent the speakers from playing sound through headphones or Bluetooth devices'),
  ('f9f064e7-97f6-58eb-bbf9-08e25c0df19e'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'A desktop monitor is turned ON, its power light is blinking, and it says "No Signal." What is the most likely practical cause?', 'The Recycle Bin is full', 'Either the CPU cabinet is OFF or the HDMI/VGA display cable between the CPU and monitor is loose', 'The internet website is down', 'Caps Lock is pressed on the keyboard', 'b', 'A desktop monitor is turned ON, its power light is blinking, and it says "No Signal." What is the most likely practical cause?', 'The computer is displaying the normal desktop, but a connected keyboard has a stuck Caps Lock indicator', 'Either the CPU cabinet is OFF or the HDMI/VGA display cable between the CPU and monitor is loose', 'The computer is correctly producing and sending its normal video signal, but the monitor''s speaker volume is completely turned down', 'The computer is sending video normally, but its browser has lost connection to every internet website'),
  ('6f26abb1-1262-5829-bc59-b7edc9cdc54f'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What is the difference between putting a laptop to "Sleep" versus "Shut Down"?', 'Sleep keeps open work ready in low-power memory for instant wake-up; Shut Down closes everything completely', 'Shut Down uses more battery than playing games', 'Both are identical', 'Sleep erases all saved files', 'a', 'What is the difference between putting a laptop to "Sleep" versus "Shut Down"?', 'Sleep keeps open work ready in low-power memory for instant wake-up; Shut Down closes everything completely', 'Sleep turns the computer off completely; Shut Down saves open work in memory so it is ready to wake again', 'Sleep closes all work and disconnects power; Shut Down keeps every program in memory for a quick wake', 'Sleep permanently erases saved documents; Shut Down stores only the desktop wallpaper between work sessions'),
  ('b8663607-5356-5338-b0e5-a717022a400d'::uuid, 12, 'Computer Hardware', 'medium', 'What does screen resolution like "1920 × 1080 (Full HD)" describe on a monitor or phone?', 'The weight of the monitor in grams', 'The grid of tiny pixels (width × height) that makes up the sharpness of the display', 'How many files can fit on the desktop', 'How loud the speakers are', 'b', 'What does screen resolution like "1920 × 1080 (Full HD)" describe on a monitor or phone?', 'The screen''s physical size measured diagonally from one corner to the opposite corner', 'The grid of tiny pixels (width × height) that makes up the sharpness of the display', 'The maximum brightness of the display at its highest setting, measured in a unit such as nits', 'The rate per second at which the display refreshes its picture while you scroll through a page'),
