  ('cb04b6f2-1c26-5a95-895b-64479a8bc487'::uuid, 12, 'Web Browsing & Internet', 'medium', 'In Chrome/Edge, why is creating separate "Browser Profiles" helpful when two siblings share one home laptop?', 'It makes Wi-Fi free', 'It creates two physical screens', 'It doubles the laptop hard disk size', 'Each sibling gets their own separate bookmarks, history, and logged-in school accounts without mixing them up', 'd', 'In Chrome/Edge, why is creating separate "Browser Profiles" helpful when two siblings share one home laptop?', 'Each profile permanently hides all its data from every other user without setting a password', 'Each profile automatically receives a second physical display connected to the shared laptop', 'Each profile doubles the laptop''s physical storage by making a separate complete copy of the full hard disk', 'Each sibling gets their own separate bookmarks, history, and logged-in school accounts without mixing them up'),
