  ('504141d4-9fdd-5fd9-86c3-a7f12280a95c'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Only to change icon colors', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'To erase your photos', 'To slow down your internet', 'b', 'Why do phones and Windows regularly release "Security Updates"?', 'Add new visual themes and icon colours even when no security flaws or software problems are being fixed', 'To patch newly discovered security holes so hackers and malware cannot exploit them', 'Remove every personal file so the device can no longer be infected by malicious attachments', 'Increase internet download speeds by replacing the Wi-Fi hardware with a faster network chip'),
  ('2fbc8707-0f2f-5ed7-9040-da450dad36fb'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Send a prank email from their account', 'Change their account password', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Read their private emails for fun', 'c', 'If a classmate accidentally left their Gmail open on a school lab computer, what is the ONLY ethical thing to do?', 'Send a harmless message from their account to inform the class, then sign out when the computer is no longer needed', 'Read a few recent emails to check whether the account is important, then sign out and tell the classmate afterward', 'Immediately click "Sign Out" without reading a single email, and politely let them know to be careful next time', 'Change the password to protect the account, then tell the classmate that the new login details are a surprise'),
  ('40e3d977-cad8-5569-b8ea-39546942b21d'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Turn off spell check', 'Never read what you submit', 'Assume computers can never be wrong', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website', 'd', 'Sometimes AI chatbots confidently make up a fake book title, date, or fact that sounds very believable. What should you do before putting AI facts into a school project?', 'Disable spell check and trust the dates, quotes and book titles whenever the AI describes them in a confident tone', 'Submit the generated text without reading it first, provided it is written in complete sentences and looks professional', 'Include the facts and dates as written, because a confident AI-generated answer never needs an independent source', 'Verify important facts, dates, and quotes from a reliable textbook or trusted official website'),
  ('0114d345-785b-54f1-96d5-bde736372cf9'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'Phones stop working after 10 PM', 'Night Wi-Fi costs double', 'Batteries charge only when silent', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning', 'd', 'Why is keeping phones on silent and putting screens away at least 30–45 minutes before sleep recommended by doctors?', 'The internal phone clock stops working permanently whenever the user looks at any screen after ten in the evening', 'Internet service always costs twice as much after 10 PM, no matter which plan the family has purchased', 'A phone can recharge only in silent mode and never charges when notification or alert sounds are on', 'Bright late-night screens and endless notifications disturb deep sleep and leave you tired in class the next morning'),
  ('65d143e3-ec68-54c8-bf3f-f4ef9253bc22'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Click every link they sent', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send them your phone number to argue back', 'Keep it secret and worry alone', 'b', 'If you receive an uncomfortable, threatening, or scam message from an unknown account online, what 3 steps protect you best?', 'Reply to the stranger in a private conversation to negotiate directly, then click all of their links so you can decide later whether to report the message', 'Do NOT reply or argue — take a screenshot as proof if needed, Block/Report the account, and tell a trusted parent or teacher', 'Send your phone number to the account to settle the argument, then wait for them to decide whether to stop sending messages', 'Keep the message private, delete the evidence immediately, and avoid telling anyone until the stranger stops contacting you'),
