  ('1855d16d-a33f-5271-94ee-13387a8d52c5'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'easy', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Twist sideways on one leg', 'Keep the monitor on the floor', 'Bend your neck 90 degrees inches from the keyboard', 'a', 'When sitting at a computer desk for an hour, what healthy posture avoids neck and back ache?', 'Sit upright with feet flat, shoulders relaxed, and top of the screen near eye level rather than hunching low', 'Bring the face very close to the keyboard and keep the elbows raised without supporting the forearms', 'Sit with a twisted back, one leg tucked under the chair, and the screen turned far to one side', 'Keep the monitor below knee height and bend the neck downward continuously while leaning very close toward the keyboard and desk'),
  ('8a4c0ba2-0af8-55fe-b567-d680dd258703'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '1930', '101', '108', '139', 'a', 'What is India’s official national Cyber Crime Helpline number (and portal `cybercrime.gov.in`) in case a family member faces online financial fraud?', '1930', '1091', '1098', '1810'),
  ('8b814afa-52bf-5730-bf5a-f655ef36137b'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'A high-resolution underwater nature video', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'An encrypted ZIP file', 'A backup stored deep inside a folder', 'b', 'What is a "Deepfake" video or voice clip that everyone on social media needs to be aware of today?', 'A high-resolution recording of an actual underwater scene that has not been altered with artificial intelligence at all', 'An AI-manipulated video or cloned voice that makes a real person appear to say or do something they NEVER actually did', 'A backup copy stored in a deeply nested folder with the original video and voice completely unchanged', 'An encrypted video that remains unchanged but requires a special key before any authorised viewer can open it'),
  ('e503fb18-2d69-590e-9a28-6aafdef6efd2'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Share bank OTPs on the call', 'Install a screen-sharing app they suggest', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Transfer money within 10 seconds in panic', 'c', 'Someone calls your parent in panic using a realistic-sounding voice saying "Send ₹10,000 urgently to this new number, don’t tell anyone!" What is the smart verification habit?', 'Share the family''s banking OTPs with the caller so that they can prove that the request is legitimate', 'Install the caller''s suggested screen-sharing app before verifying who is asking for the money', 'Pause, hang up, and call the family member directly on their REAL known phone number to verify before sending a rupee!', 'Transfer the money immediately to the unfamiliar number, then call the family member on their known phone to check the request'),
  ('9b6890b8-1962-5265-aeb8-47b68a76dc20'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'Banks require AnyDesk for every account', 'To double your mobile battery life', 'To clean dust from your phone speaker', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!', 'd', 'Why do scammers urgently ask victims to install remote screen-sharing apps (like AnyDesk / TeamViewer / unknown `.apk`s) during fake "KYC / customer care" calls?', 'A caller can verify your identity safely only by controlling your device, even when you did not initiate the call', 'The app gives the caller no control or information and guarantees that your banking activity remains private', 'A shared screen prevents the other person from seeing notifications, banking apps and one-time passcodes', 'Because screen-sharing lets the scammer see your live phone screen, including incoming bank OTPs and apps!'),
  ('44f7245d-8ca1-586c-a2ee-2ece8afb5f9d'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Parents’ bank account numbers and Aadhaar passwords', 'Home Wi-Fi passwords of every student', 'Personal email passwords', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!', 'd', 'When designing a club registration form (Data Minimization principle), which information is ethical and sensible to collect?', 'Collect parents'' bank account details, private identity credentials and financial information even though the club does not need it', 'Collect every student''s home Wi-Fi password so the club can access the family''s router whenever necessary', 'Collect the password for each student''s personal email account to simplify future club announcements', 'Only what is genuinely needed for the club (Name, Roll No, Class, Section) — never unnecessary private family/financial data!'),
  ('9e00da3c-e202-5654-a619-2123e87499f6'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'Nobody is allowed to view the image', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The file contains a virus', 'You can sell it as your own painting without credit', 'b', 'What does a "Creative Commons (CC)" license on an online photo or music track tell students making a video project?', 'The license prevents anyone from viewing the work, even if the creator has posted it on a public webpage', 'The creator has given clear permission to reuse the work under stated conditions (such as giving proper attribution/credit)', 'The license automatically makes every work public domain and allows all personal and commercial uses without any restrictions or attribution whatsoever', 'The license allows you to claim that you created the work and remove any required credits from the finished video'),
  ('e4262bb6-b354-52de-ba1e-632cfcd97dc9'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'medium', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break screens with a hammer in class', 'Burn plastic circuit boards in the backyard', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water', 'Throw batteries into rivers', 'c', 'What should families do with old dead batteries, broken chargers, and discarded electronics ("E-Waste") instead of burning them or tossing them in open drains?', 'Break the screens into smaller pieces in the classroom and mix all of the sharp fragments with ordinary school waste', 'Burn the plastic circuit boards and cable coverings outdoors so that the remaining metal can be stored at home', 'Hand them over to authorized E-Waste collection/recycling centers so toxic metals don’t pollute soil and water', 'Throw old batteries into a river or drain and assume that the water will safely dissolve their contents'),
  ('8768b91d-280b-5c9e-95ec-63d9dbf09ee9'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Why do social media "recommendation algorithms" create an "Echo Chamber" if you are not mindful?', 'They keep showing more of whatever you clicked before, which can make one-sided opinions or rumors look like the whole truth', 'They delete posts older than 1 hour', 'They turn off Wi-Fi in closed rooms', 'They make your phone speaker echo loudly', 'a', 'Why do social media "recommendation algorithms" create an "Echo Chamber" if you are not mindful?', 'They keep showing more of whatever you clicked before, which can make one-sided opinions or rumors look like the whole truth', 'Algorithms show every possible opinion in the same fixed proportion regardless of what the user clicks, shares, follows or watches on the platform', 'Algorithms stop recommending content whenever a person follows several accounts with the same point of view', 'Algorithms delete every post older than one hour, preventing anyone from reading earlier opinions or discussions'),
  ('8ec696e5-c781-5c8b-b21a-a80af29fbe2d'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'Before posting a close-up photo of your house keys, boarding pass barcode, or school exam admit card barcode publicly on Instagram/status, why should you pause?', 'Visible QR codes, barcodes, roll/application IDs, and personal details in photos can be scanned and misused by strangers!', 'Barcodes blur camera lenses', 'Social media bans white paper', 'There is no privacy risk at all', 'a', 'Before posting a close-up photo of your house keys, boarding pass barcode, or school exam admit card barcode publicly on Instagram/status, why should you pause?', 'Visible QR codes, barcodes, roll/application IDs, and personal details in photos can be scanned and misused by strangers!', 'Photos of keys and codes cannot expose usable information unless the original paper document or metal key is stolen', 'Only a person''s full name can reveal private information, so barcodes, roll numbers and identification details can always be posted safely online', 'Any image is safe to post publicly if it disappears from a social media story after the standard time limit'),
  ('e18d09cd-0f09-58bf-904d-c7caf48e50ce'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What is "Ransomware", and what single everyday habit best protects your school/home projects against it?', 'A free antivirus tool from Microsoft', 'Malware that locks files and demands money — keeping regular offline/cloud backups and avoiding shady downloads protects you!', 'A fast fiber router', 'A type of gaming keyboard', 'b', 'What is "Ransomware", and what single everyday habit best protects your school/home projects against it?', 'A free antivirus product that encrypts files as a normal backup; protection means sharing its key with anyone who asks', 'Malware that locks files and demands money — keeping regular offline/cloud backups and avoiding shady downloads protects you!', 'A router feature that speeds up every network; protecting work means never saving a copy to another drive or account, regardless of how important the files are', 'A gaming keyboard that disconnects the computer from a screen; protection means cleaning all of its keys once a month'),
  ('ba76073c-5774-54b8-b12f-641f9290d0c5'::uuid, 12, 'Social Ethics & Cyber Safety', 'hard', 'What does true "Accessibility" mean when students build a website or poster for the school community?', 'Making buttons 2 pixels small', 'Locking the site so nobody can open it', 'Using clear readable fonts, strong color contrast, and image descriptions (`alt` text) so everyone — including people with low vision — can use it comfortably', 'Using tiny light-yellow text on a white background', 'c', 'What does true "Accessibility" mean when students build a website or poster for the school community?', 'Making every control depend on precise mouse movements and not providing labels or alternative text for people using a keyboard or a screen reader', 'Using small decorative fonts and low-contrast colours for a consistent appearance even if users with low vision find the text difficult to read or navigate on a computer or phone', 'Using clear readable fonts, strong color contrast, and image descriptions (`alt` text) so everyone — including people with low vision — can use it comfortably', 'Restricting the site to one preferred device and hiding captions and text descriptions to make the page appear simpler for most visitors');
